n_petclinic/commit/c52f0c024c42dbe0b7d9646bbd80667fe5622a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGM1MmYwYzAyNGM0MmRiZTBiN2Q5NjQ2YmJkODA2NjdmZTU2MjJhOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/674f018dfd9129729163b55da4102d0abce1395b","sha":"674f018dfd9129729163b55da4102d0abce1395b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/674f018dfd9129729163b55da4102d0abce1395b"}],"sha":"c52f0c024c42dbe0b7d9646bbd80667fe5622a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/c52f0c024c42dbe0b7d9646bbd80667fe5622a8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107361953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikegents","id":107361953,"login":"mikegents","node_id":"U_kgDOBmY2oQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/674f018dfd9129729163b55da4102d0abce1395b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:45:23Z","email":"107361953+mikegents@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mike Gents"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:45:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(PROD-CPC-2039) Fix ReleaseDate autofill on product update page (#1575)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[[PROD-CPC-2039](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2039)\n\n## Context\n\nThe product update form did not autofill the product’s existing release\ndate. Although the release date was stored, it was missing from the\nresponse models used by the Products Service and API Gateway. As a\nresult, the employee frontend received no release date and displayed an\nempty field.\n\n## Does this PR change the `.vscode` folder in `petclinic-frontend`?\n\nNo. This PR does not change the `.vscode` folder.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `releaseDate` to the Products Service `ProductResponseModel`.\n- Added `releaseDate` to the API Gateway `ProductResponseDTO`.\n- Updated the API Gateway DTO constructor to pass the release date\nthrough.\n- The employee frontend can now receive the saved release date and\nautofill it in the product update form.\n- No frontend source files were changed.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\n\nNo. This change updates fields in the existing product response flow and\ndoes not introduce or require a new v2 API endpoint.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo. It only adds an existing product field to the responses sent through\nthe current Products Service → API Gateway → employee frontend flow. No\nC4 L2 update is required.\n\n## Dev notes\n\nThe release date was already accepted and persisted by the backend. The\nissue was that it was omitted from both backend response DTOs,\npreventing it from reaching the frontend.\n\n## Linked pull requests\n\nNone.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nathan Bessette <123912175+NateDev5@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: AarushP06 <167229698+AarushP06@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b6f90616cdbfd02f7312fb9b34e9016cb6c3a7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/5b6f90616cdbfd02f7312fb9b34e9016cb6c3a7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/674f018dfd9129729163b55da4102d0abce1395b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b6f90616cdbfd02f7312fb9b34e9016cb6c3a7b\nparent 0df5729fe1912f8fd25b062d153f003cf0fcc90e\nauthor Mike Gents <107361953+mikegents@users.noreply.github.com> 1791384323 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791384323 -0400\n\nbug(PROD-CPC-2039) Fix ReleaseDate autofill on product update page (#1575)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[[PROD-CPC-2039](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2039)\n\n## Context\n\nThe product update form did not autofill the product’s existing release\ndate. Although the release date was stored, it was missing from the\nresponse models used by the Products Service and API Gateway. As a\nresult, the employee frontend received no release date and displayed an\nempty field.\n\n## Does this PR change the `.vscode` folder in `petclinic-frontend`?\n\nNo. This PR does not change the `.vscode` folder.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `releaseDate` to the Products Service `ProductResponseModel`.\n- Added `releaseDate` to the API Gateway `ProductResponseDTO`.\n- Updated the API Gateway DTO constructor to pass the release date\nthrough.\n- The employee frontend can now receive the saved release date and\nautofill it in the product update form.\n- No frontend source files were changed.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\n\nNo. This change updates fields in the existing product response flow and\ndoes not introduce or require a new v2 API endpoint.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo. It only adds an existing product field to the responses sent through\nthe current Products Service → API Gateway → employee frontend flow. No\nC4 L2 update is required.\n\n## Dev notes\n\nThe release date was already accepted and persisted by the backend. The\nissue was that it was omitted from both backend response DTOs,\npreventing it from reaching the frontend.\n\n## Linked pull requests\n\nNone.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nathan Bessette <123912175+NateDev5@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by