c/commits/6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff"}],"sha":"0df5729fe1912f8fd25b062d153f003cf0fcc90e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/0df5729fe1912f8fd25b062d153f003cf0fcc90e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208994289?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rainarra","id":208994289,"login":"rainarra","node_id":"U_kgDODHT_8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:36:07Z","email":"awintle@hotmail.com","name":"Alexandra wintle"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:36:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-2053): redesign edit pet experience (#1580)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CUST-CPC-2053]https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/14?selectedIssue=CPC-2053\n\n## Context:\nThis ticket redesigns the customer pet editing experience. Previously,\nediting a pet used a separate edit flow/modal. The new design allows\ncustomers to edit their pet directly from the customer profile without\nnavigating to a separate page.\n\nThe goal is to make editing a pet more direct and easier to use while\npreserving the existing pet update, validation, deletion, and photo\nfunctionality.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo. This PR does not make any changes to the `.vscode` folder.\n\n\n## Changes\n- Replaced the separate pet editing flow with an inline edit form\ndisplayed directly within the customer profile.\n- Updated `CustomerDetails` to display `UpdatePetForm` when a pet is\nselected for editing.\n- Updated `CustomerProfilePage` to support inline pet editing.\n- Updated `UpdatePetForm` to handle the pet editing, validation, update,\ndelete, and cancel actions within the profile.\n- Removed the separate `UpdateCustomerPetPage` flow.\n- Updated `ProfilePage` and routing to support the redesigned\nprofile/edit flow.\n- Preserved existing pet validation and update functionality.\n- Existing pet photo and deletion functionality remains available.\n- Changes are limited to the customer/CUST frontend functionality.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. This PR does not introduce or migrate functionality to the v2 API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This PR does not add any new communication between services and does\nnot require changes to the C4 L2 diagram.\n\n## Before and After UI \n\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"472\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cfae0e53-dfe0-46a4-a720-744c46077d13\"\n/>\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"469\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/702920ea-2901-4081-b198-d29edbd3e006\"\n/>\n\n\nThe previous implementation used a separate pet editing flow/modal.\n\n### After\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"548\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6ef70c7-4988-45ec-b879-022520485752\"\n/>\n\n\nThe new implementation displays the pet editing form directly within the\ncustomer profile, allowing the customer to edit the pet without\nnavigating away from the profile.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- The previous separate `UpdateCustomerPetPage` was removed as it is no\nlonger required for the new edit page.\n- Manual testing was performed for editing, saving, cancelling,\ndeleting, refreshing the profile, and verifying that updated pet\ninformation persists ( everything saved properly)\n- `npm run lint` passes.\n- `npm run build` passes.\n\n\n\n\nRequested visual update:\n\nchanges: active button is now smaller and doesn''t have a line of its own\ndelete and cancel button are now spaced and colour coded\n\n<img width=\"856\" height=\"430\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4933c23-0107-47fd-815b-971f2a1bf888\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"7c898ac0f043f664e78e446b9a167605d01e474b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/7c898ac0f043f664e78e446b9a167605d01e474b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c898ac0f043f664e78e446b9a167605d01e474b\nparent a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987\nauthor Alexandra wintle <awintle@hotmail.com> 1791340567 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791340567 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-2053): redesign edit pet experience (#1580)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CUST-CPC-2053]https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/14?selectedIssue=CPC-2053\n\n## Context:\nThis ticket redesigns the customer pet editing experience. Previously,\nediting a pet used a separate edit flow/modal. The new design allows\ncustomers to edit their pet directly from the customer profile without\nnavigating to a separate page.\n\nThe goal is to make editing a pet more direct and easier to use while\npreserving the existing pet update, validation, deletion, and photo\nfunctionality.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo. This PR does not make any changes to the `.vscode` folder.\n\n\n## Changes\n- Replaced the separate pet editing flow with an inline edit form\ndisplayed directly within the customer profile.\n- Updated `CustomerDetails` to display `UpdatePetForm` when a pet is\nselected for editing.\n- Updated `CustomerProfilePage` to support inline pet editing.\n- Updated `UpdatePetForm` to handle the pet editing, validation, update,\ndelete, and cancel actions within the profile.\n- Removed the separate `UpdateCustomerPetPage` flow.\n- Updated `ProfilePage` and routing to support the redesigned\nprofile/edit flow.\n- Preserved existing pet validation and update functionality.\n- Existing pet photo and deletion functionality remains available.\n- Changes are limited to the customer/CUST frontend functionality.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. This PR does not introduce or migrate functionality to the v2 API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This PR does not add any new communication between services and does\nnot require changes to the C4 L2 diagram.\n\n## Before and After UI \n\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"472\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cfae0e53-dfe0-46a4-a720-744c46077d13\"\n/>\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"469\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/702920ea-2901-4081-b198-d29edbd3e006\"\n/>\n\n\nThe previous implementation used a separate pet editing flow/modal.\n\n### After\n<img width=\"975\" height=\"548\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6ef70c7-4988-45ec-b879-022520485752\"\n/>\n\n\nThe new implementation displays the pet editing form directly within the\ncustomer profile, allowing the customer to edit the pet without\nnavigating away from the profile.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- The previous separate `UpdateCustomerPetPage` was removed as it is no\nlonger required for the new edit page.\n- Manual testing was performed for editing, saving, cancelling,\ndeleting, refreshing the profile, and verifying that updated pet\ninformation persists ( everything saved properly)\n- `npm run lint` passes.\n- `npm run build` passes.\n\n\n\n\nRequested visual update:\n\nchanges: active button is now smaller and doesn''t have a line of its own\ndelete and cancel button are now spaced and colour coded\n\n<img width=\"856\" height=\"430\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4933c23-0107-47fd-815b-971f2a1bf888\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxbAXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAruUQAFlOIX34g8PDRgcAQLU0QYNT\nHeZlOGqd6I9H3qOi+TcAMX1jqqZGfatC+UK3HMVNxHgr3oTE6/lLfRn1hxPMFWEL\nbYBjwyaAC9m/Dkl3POygLh1NXKVfzTnGfWxQn77kwzU7+dQWiDOMhoibWC1tlTKP\njyvq1RWjD0cfGJRN/BLtAuGQY1VGa2KqPP4s4waY1lG3cix13XoA6fr+2X4Upx35\nu5F5b2GCWgGsuoWUiKHmqSz47VFopG5AD1U/I6UjRiGzSlMlxyQ3mMMdKB+rWEOY\nns33BA87rRTmi1FFARo+lz0cmYiEihjzx2VLVEilfYrTZbShaxVXa2K29EjdPtEm\n/fHA7RA4jmH0qqsC+9Xo8lyrfH66lqnvc1Z9mimLXLZ6gP+7TTfuah7Zgm/WP6wy\nIg1LTRkTb7WYmzhm1A4q6w+6IjGIqksYaqe3z14tQSYZLkO2GV/pk3AicYA/j93w\nbk9w4dcvg2zWg05u35lJZ2SYcZ8rj2/OMb8lr3VSP0AKP68dYP7WGOJSTrwNR4iE\nfz5vmM8qXSQFHZtRmtVaxDx9qA/+h99xHSlcdZeN/6d8Wd0JxoKmaWnD2nGuXmNC\nAWO3NuMRFFsQ50ff0c0sB5kD66nAqzugPR+sMS8BfDWueQ5YvnGsyOamvnBIZo/N\nwYRN51CawHSye0I7N8l1\n=b0V8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T02:36:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDZmZGRmYmRkYWY5NjRmYmY1Zjc1ZWMwNTNlY2MxMzkzYzY4ZWEwZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987","sha":"a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987"}],"sha":"6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/6fddfbddaf964fbf5f75ec053ecc1393c68ea0ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167229700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cauealDEV","id":167229700,"login":"cauealDEV","node_id":"U_kgDOCfe5BA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cauealDEV","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:07:44Z","email":"167229700+cauealDEV@users.noreply.github.com","name":"caueal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:07:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VETS-CPC-2100): Localization for employee portal vet page (#1582)\n\n**JIRA:** link to jira ticket\n## Context:\nLocalize the Veterinarians page (veterinarians.html) in the\nemployee-frontend project. This change ensures that the page follows the\nproject''s internationalization (i18n) standards by embedding hardcoded\nbase text in French and attaching native Angular i18n=\"@@key\" attributes\nto allow dynamic switching to English via public/i18n/en.json.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo, this PR does not touch or modify the .vscode folder.\n\n## Changes\nsrc/app/features/vets/pages/veterinarians/veterinarians.html:\n\n- Converted all user-facing template text (headings, descriptions,\nbuttons, and status badges) to base French.\n\n- Added native Angular i18n=\"@@vets.*\" key attributes to all text nodes\nfor dynamic translation.\n\n- Verified translation mappings in public/i18n/en.json.\nNo other frontend modules or backend services were affected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nWhen it goes to /vets, it shows in French first:\n<img width=\"1828\" height=\"967\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d4bdf2d-b4c7-4f9b-8138-974eb0ef754e\"\n/>\n\nAfter toggling the button, it translates to English:\n<img width=\"1762\" height=\"942\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b427879b-577d-40b3-bedd-ad052956364f\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nFollows the Angular native i18n=\"@@key\" standard, requiring no custom TS\ndirective imports inside veterinarians.ts.\nVerified runtime language switching manually in browser.\nExisting test suite failures (header.spec.ts, inventory-list.spec.ts,\nsupply-page.spec.ts) were confirmed to be pre-existing mock issues\nunrelated to this feature branch.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nN/A\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: JackyKBK <2331914@champlaincollege.qc.ca>\nCo-authored-by: JackyB <167229877+JackyKBK@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Chin-Yi <chinyi615@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Viktoria Zlateva <zlateva.vik@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vikit <Vikit@VIK_LAP>\nCo-authored-by: caczzx <167229700+caczzx@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d3ae420a3f35f25e0072129d36c1a421e835adc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/9d3ae420a3f35f25e0072129d36c1a421e835adc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/a07a276c2886994179b51e63479fe0e0bf1b2987","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d3ae420a3f35f25e0072129d36c1a421e835adc\nparent 675adbf67990c3bf35bf610019d7569a32e6492b\nauthor caueal <167229700+cauealDEV@users.noreply.github.com> 1791338864 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791338864 -0400\n\nfeat(VETS-CPC-2100): Localization for employee portal vet page (#1582)\n\n**JIRA:** link to jira ticket\n## Context:\nLocalize the Veterinarians page (veterinarians.html) in the\nemployee-frontend project. This change ensures that the page follows the\nproject''s internationalization (i18n) standards by embedding hardcoded\nbase text in French and attaching native Angular i18n=\"@@key\" attributes\nto allow dynamic switching to English via public/i18n/en.json.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo, this PR does not touch or modify the .vscode folder.\n\n## Changes\nsrc/app/features/vets/pages/veterinarians/veterinarians.html:\n\n- Converted all user-facing template text (headings, descriptions,\nbuttons, and status badges) to base French.\n\n- Added native Angular i18n=\"@@vets.*\" key attributes to all text nodes\nfor dynamic translation.\n\n- Verified translation mappings in public/i18n/en.json.\nNo other frontend modules or backend services were affected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nWhen it goes to /vets, it shows in French first:\n<img width=\"1828\" height=\"967\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d4bdf2d-b4c7-4f9b-8138-974eb0ef754e\"\n/>\n\nAfter toggling the button, it translates to English:\n<img width=\"1762\" height=\"942\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b427879b-577d-40b3-bedd-ad052956364f\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nFollows the Angular native i18n=\"@@key\" standard, requiring no custom TS\ndirective imports inside veterinarians.ts.\nVerified runtime language switching manually in browser.\nExisting test suite failures (header.spec.ts, inventory-list.spec.ts,\nsupply-page.spec.ts) were confirmed to be pre-existing mock issues\nunrelated to this feature branch.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nN/A\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: JackyKBK <2331914@champlaincollege.qc.ca>\nCo-authored-by: JackyB <167229877+JackyKBK@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Chin-Yi <chinyi615@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Viktoria Zlateva <zlateva.vik@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vikit <Vikit@VIK_LAP>\nCo-authored-by: caczzx <167229700+caczzx@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxalwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1W8QABe1sTod7JRyGEuwagQ6RyFu\nAq8VUjCIVQiKPsg2KODneRLs1S4N5PIe6VVq1Wo7OYPF1hO9+HYgwVdzyjzRmo7G\nR9th620p3BNG/pGjnrYPbTu8Jehm9uYhCVqrOk+0Zz+o8xG5JUE/6PNCzVM8DzPZ\nttfk0DaAVidmRBdiQwLEog9yCyew+GjSiRQfgZMQGYJAJEgvkunCO22ohUhtFC3l\nZcp3as3DcKJVzZ5QPS37YDpVxw7MKtVgJnLXoYHv/YH5uwP79WCsMjAdl9QzckbY\nhNCEpWo5lWk+fpS1ZLiH46qnw3BihqYP1k6NGCogzUzjNGirplOeMms3O01W6EIm\najY8Q9rMJl/L8zeosvkDEoRREZogOFQ5S2K9YPyW4WPx5yM3T2o