39a6c771f8812858"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152046888?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Malick-Konate","id":152046888,"login":"Malick-Konate","node_id":"U_kgDOCRANKA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Malick-Konate","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/8a71732c665395689c39f53c4d3a0603c0716046/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:50:55Z","email":"152046888+Malick-Konate@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Malick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T21:50:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(INVT-CPC-1958/1959/1960/1974): role-based dynamic inventory changes (#1536)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1958\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1974\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1960\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1959\n\n## Context:\nAn employee''s inventory page should show different capabilities\ndepending\non their role. Admin and Inventory_Manager get full CRUD on inventories\nand products, Vet gets read access plus the ability to consume a\nproduct,\nand Receptionist currently has no gateway access to inventory data at\nall\n(confirmed directly against `api-gateway`''s `@SecuredEndpoint` rules,\nnot\njust the ticket text).\n\n**Note on branch structure:** these four tickets (CPC-1958, 1974, 1959,\n1960) are combined on one branch/PR, which goes against the one-branch-\nper-ticket convention from Sprint Kickoff. The reasoning was that all\nfour\nreduce to the exact same code. Admin and Inventory_Manager are\nfunctionally identical at the gateway level (no endpoint distinguishes\nthem), and Vet/Receptionist are strict subsets of that same page''s\nbehavior — so there''s no actual separate implementation per ticket, only\none shared permissions map (`inventory-permissions.ts`) applied to one\npage.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Added `shared/models/inventory-permissions.ts` — a role → capability\nmap, grounded in the actual `@SecuredEndpoint(allowedRoles = ...)` rules\n  in `api-gateway`''s `InventoryControllerV1`, not just the ticket text.\n- `inventory-list.ts` / `.html`: wired the permissions map in —\n  Receptionist never opens the inventory SSE stream at all (shown a\nrestricted-access message instead), and Vet never calls `getQuantity()`\n  (that endpoint is Admin/Inventory_Manager only at the gateway level).\n- Added an inline Add/Edit/Delete Inventory form (not a modal — see Dev\n  notes) so the CRUD acceptance criteria for CPC-1958/1974 are actually\n  testable, gated by `can().canCreateInventory` /\n  `can().canUpdateInventory` / `can().canDeleteInventory`.\n- Inventory type is now a dropdown (Bandages / Injections / Medications\n/\n  Equipment) instead of free text, to avoid inconsistent values on new\n  inventories.\n- `inventory-service.ts`: added `createInventory`, `updateInventory`,\n`deleteInventory`, `getInventoryById`. Also fixed a pre-existing bug in\n  `getInventoryById`''s SSE call. It was only passing 3 arguments to\n  `stream()` instead of 4, so `''GET''` was landing in the headers-object\n  parameter position instead of the method position.\n- `inventory.model.ts`: added `InventoryRequest` and an `InventoryType`\n  union for the four allowed values.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. uses the existing v1 gateway endpoint (InventoryControllerV1), just\nwidening its allowedRoles to include VET\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Admin / Inventory_Manager** — full view with Edit/Delete actions:\n<img width=\"826\" height=\"482\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b1cdaac-d023-4431-aa24-9ce85e3e9b05\"\n/>\n\n**Edit form:**\n<img width=\"783\" height=\"372\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b332db0-feb4-4104-8ee1-26d78ad133e8\"\n/>\n\n**Vet** — list view, no quantities, no edit/delete actions:\n<img width=\"770\" height=\"578\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/565954dd-d710-43db-9565-d8314c6e8cbf\"\n/>\n\n**Receptionist** — restricted-access message, no API call made:\n<img width=\"778\" height=\"480\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3a61110-2046-45f2-974e-78368e9e287e\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nPermissions are enforced twice: hidden/disabled in the UI here, and\nindependently rejected with a 403 by `api-gateway`''s `RoleFilter` if\ncalled directly this PR only handles the UI half; the backend\nenforcement already exists and isn''t part of this change.\n\nThe Add/Edit Inventory form here is a plain inline form, not a modal.\nCPC-1958/1974''s CRUD criteria need a working form to test against, and\nthe separate \"Use modals for Inventory action forms\" ticket''s own\nacceptance criteria assume one already exists to wrap so this form\nexists now, and swapping it into a modal later shouldn''t require\ntouching the underlying create/update/delete logic, only where it\nrenders.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n#1490 (merged — this PR builds directly on top of it)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: LazaroESV <lazarosagarra18@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"92c7422341db0e8bf5b34d043d193ff40eecdef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/92c7422341db0e8bf5b34d043d193ff40eecdef2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/8a71732c665395689c39f53c4d3a0603c0716046","verification":{"payload":"tree 92c7422341db0e8bf5b34d043d193ff40eecdef2\nparent a67a08d1e4b5a76e867c516e236f4ff26fa74d41\nauthor Malick <152046888+Malick-Konate@users.noreply.github.com> 1791323455 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791323455 -0400\n\nfeat(INVT-CPC-1958/1959/1960/1974): role-based dynamic inventory changes (#1536)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1958\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1974\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1960\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1959\n\n## Context:\nAn employee''s inventory page should show different capabilities\ndepending\non their role. Admin and Inventory_Manager get full CRUD on inventories\nand products, Vet gets read access plus the ability to consume a\nproduct,\nand Receptionist currently has no gateway access to inventory data at\nall\n(confirmed directly against `api-gateway`''s `@SecuredEndpoint` rules,\nnot\njust the ticket text).\n\n**Note on branch structure:** these four tickets (CPC-1958, 1974, 1959,\n1960) are combined on one branch/PR, which goes against the one-branch-\nper-ticket convention from Sprint Kickoff. The reasoning was that all\nfour\nreduce to the exact same code. Admin and Inventory_Manager are\nfunctionally identical at the gateway level (no endpoint distinguishes\nthem), and Vet/Receptionist are strict subsets of that same page''s\nbehavior — so there''s no actual separate implementation per ticket, only\none shared permissions map (`inventory-permissions.ts`) applied to one\npage.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Added `shared/models/inventory-permissions.ts` — a role → capability\nmap, grounded in the actual `@SecuredEndpoint(allowedRoles = ...)` rules\n  in `api-gateway`''s `InventoryControllerV1`, not just the ticket text.\n- `inventory-list.ts` / `.html`: wired the permissions map in —\n  Receptionist never opens the inventory SSE stream at all (shown a\nrestricted-access message instead), and Vet never calls `getQuantity()`\n  (that endpoint is Admin/Inventory_Manager only at the gateway level).\n- Added an inline Add/Edit/Delete Inventory form (not a modal — see Dev\n  notes) so the CRUD acceptance criteria for CPC-1958/1974 are actually\n  testable, gated by `can().canCreateInventory` /\n  `can().canUpdateInventory` / `can().canDeleteInventory`.\n- Inventory type is now a dropdown (Bandages / Injections / Medications\n/\n  Equipment) instead of free text, to avoid inconsistent values on new\n  inventories.\n- `inventory-service.ts`: added `createInventory`, `updateInventory`,\n`deleteInventory`, `getInventoryById`. Also fixed a pre-existing bug in\n  `getInventoryById`''s SSE call. It was only passing 3 arguments to\n  `stream()` instead of 4, so `''GET''` was landing in the headers-object\n  parameter position instead of the method position.\n- `inventory.model.ts`: added `InventoryRequest` and an `InventoryType`\n  union for the four allowed values.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. uses the existing v1 gateway endpoint (InventoryControllerV1), just\nwidening its allowedRoles to include VET\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Admin / Inventory_Manager** — full view with Edit/Delete actions:\n<img width=\"826\" height=\"482\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b1cdaac-d023-4431-aa24-9ce85e3e9b05\"\n/>\n\n**Edit form:**\n<img width=\"783\" height=\"372\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b332db0-feb4-4104-8ee1-26d78ad133e8\"\n/>\n\n**Vet** — list view, no quantities, no edit/delete actions:\n<img width=\"770\" height=\"578\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/565954dd-d710-43db-9565-d8314c6e8cbf\"\n/>\n\n**Receptionist** — restricted-access message, no API call made:\n<img width=\"778\" height=\"480\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3a61110-2046-45f2-974e-78368e9e287e\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nPermissions are enforced twice: hidden/disabled in the UI here, and\nindependently rejected with a 403 by `api-gateway`''s `RoleFilter` if\ncalled directly this PR only handles the UI half; the backend\nenforcement already exists and isn''t part of this change.\n\nThe Add/Edit Inventory form here is a plain inline form, not a modal.\nCPC-1958/1974''s CRUD criteria need a working form to test against, and\nthe separate \"Use modals for Inventory action forms\" ticket''s own\nacceptance criteria assume one already exists to wrap so this form\nexists now, and swapping it into a modal later shouldn''t require\ntouching the underlying create/update/delete logic, only where it\nrenders.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n#1490 (merged — this PR builds directly on top of it)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: LazaroESV <lazarosagarra18@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxW0/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAm8QAH/s/gJYceWf4CuTx+63u5Hj\npM0r8ASvdtOqAN0LLWBCLZDVNohn+i9YYrcIUpXbDpI65Qbt5h6wH97Sfk9qtOEr\nxtBztipb42IfMEuuqH34AK7rw5G7uqzY9afIZ4HyOmIiYoib9ja9EEBMhrySYoGV\nyc7cKarGGd44vChKHPkHU7ca2xf46vQnyweWgZAkIu8rYymVUwQf9QhJiPmpHQ4q\n+1PXqifcBUTM2IpKokDnJCv/BPz2oKGHQxRrN80Ns+rdS1PhDgqaxdovzfoMfRMy\nxWPud5IFTDx34iBlDpuXjexp636MKBBlZ7eUurWOd/ECBHthyBa3QyuC7FpjxbcG\nrum+Empej5GUqjR3KSEAZT5S1V6vYXZQqgQhImF7IA+Dw4R57GP9hqxDRNUAJq4y\n5DXkwvpHNGHqa2y7FTbzl58TCp3UiltW0