late (#1574)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2089\n\n## Context:\n\nCPC-2089 asks for a settings page so a vet has one place to manage their\nprivate information.\n\nThis ticket delivers the template only: the page, its two sections, the\nnavigation between them, and the Save / Cancel actions, all localized in\nFrench and English. The content of each section is deliberately out of\nscope and comes with the follow-up tickets, starting with CPC-2090\n(security: password change and private documents) that I will do just\nafter. Keeping the split this way because this ticket blocks also the\nticket of the implementation of the display feature in the setting page.\nBefore this change, `/settings` rendered a `Coming soon` placeholder.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo. \n\n## Changes\n\n**Settings page** — `employee-frontend/src/app/features/settings/pages/`\n\n- replaced the `Coming soon` placeholder with the page template:\nheading, a card holding a two-column layout, and the actions row\n- left-hand section nav with `Security` and `Display`; the page opens on\n`Security`, being the first section\n- both panels are intentionally empty\n- `Save` confirms with a `MatSnackBar` (2 s, top position) and returns\nto `/home`; `Cancel` returns to `/home`\n- the actions row is the last element of the page, as the ticket\nrequires\n\n**Routing** — `employee-frontend/src/app/app.routes.ts`\n\n- the `settings` route now declares `canActivate: [authGuard(),\ncustomerRedirectGuard, employeeGuard]`, the same set the Shell applies.\n.\n\n**Localization** — `employee-frontend/public/i18n/en.json`,\n`src/app/app.config.ts`\n\n- the English catalogue is now grouped by feature instead of one flat\nlist of keys, so it stays readable as it grows\n\n- `flattenTranslations()` added to `app.config.ts`: it walks the grouped\ncatalogue and rebuilds the dotted message ids before\n`loadTranslations()` sees them.. It is made for the new english\ncatalogue in en.json because I changed the structure of it as metionned\nearlier\n\n**Documentation** — `docs/i18n-angular-usage.md`\n\n- updated for the grouped catalogue: the overview section, the folder\nmap, the worked example, the key rules, the testing notes, two new\ntroubleshooting rows, and the developer checklist\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/features/settings/pages/settings.spec.ts`\n(new): the page, its section navigation, both actions, and the\nlocalization of the template and of the snack bar message\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/app.config.spec.ts`: three unit cases for\n`flattenTranslations()`, plus one integration case that feeds the loader\na grouped catalogue and checks the English actually renders\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/app.routes.spec.ts` (new): the settings\nroute declares its guards\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n<!--\nPaste four screenshots here, in this order. Drag and drop them into the\n    GitHub form, it uploads them and inserts the markdown for you.\n\n    1. BEFORE  - /settings showing the \"Coming soon\" placeholder\n    2. AFTER   - the page in French, on the Security section\n    3. AFTER   - the page in English, to show the localization\n4. AFTER - the home page with the \"Changes saved\" snack bar visible,\n                 right after clicking Save\n\n    Keep the headings below so reviewers can tell them apart.\n-->\n\nNew UI feature: before this PR, `/settings` rendered the shared `Coming\nsoon`\nplaceholder and there was no settings UI to compare against\n\n**After — French**\n<img width=\"1890\" height=\"826\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58c038db-4e73-4fa9-89e0-19a3b4118895\"\n/>\n\n\n**After — English**\n<img width=\"1896\" height=\"831\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9fb4a97-797f-4843-b17a-c669890d0a0b\"\n/>\n\n**After — confirmation on save**\n<img width=\"1898\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9c70016-8cf6-40b0-a960-02045a13d5e8\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"aebd59dd6e37fb30f8dc444becbb1b3735da4e41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/aebd59dd6e37fb30f8dc444becbb1b3735da4e41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/fe4694029f6657ad690f71bce87e522a9a3439ed","verification":{"payload":"tree aebd59dd6e37fb30f8dc444becbb1b3735da4e41\nparent f21b4dc5c38b1fa008bde1c257147841ab706846\nauthor LKBSM <loukmanebessam@gmail.com> 1791166979 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791166979 -0400\n\nFeat/vets cpc 2089 create setting page template (#1574)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2089\n\n## Context:\n\nCPC-2089 asks for a settings page so a vet has one place to manage their\nprivate information.\n\nThis ticket delivers the template only: the page, its two sections, the\nnavigation between them, and the Save / Cancel actions, all localized in\nFrench and English. The content of each section is deliberately out of\nscope and comes with the follow-up tickets, starting with CPC-2090\n(security: password change and private documents) that I will do just\nafter. Keeping the split this way because this ticket blocks also the\nticket of the implementation of the display feature in the setting page.\nBefore this change, `/settings` rendered a `Coming soon` placeholder.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo. \n\n## Changes\n\n**Settings page** — `employee-frontend/src/app/features/settings/pages/`\n\n- replaced the `Coming soon` placeholder with the page template:\nheading, a card holding a two-column layout, and the actions row\n- left-hand section nav with `Security` and `Display`; the page opens on\n`Security`, being the first section\n- both panels are intentionally empty\n- `Save` confirms with a `MatSnackBar` (2 s, top position) and returns\nto `/home`; `Cancel` returns to `/home`\n- the actions row is the last element of the page, as the ticket\nrequires\n\n**Routing** — `employee-frontend/src/app/app.routes.ts`\n\n- the `settings` route now declares `canActivate: [authGuard(),\ncustomerRedirectGuard, employeeGuard]`, the same set the Shell applies.\n.\n\n**Localization** — `employee-frontend/public/i18n/en.json`,\n`src/app/app.config.ts`\n\n- the English catalogue is now grouped by feature instead of one flat\nlist of keys, so it stays readable as it grows\n\n- `flattenTranslations()` added to `app.config.ts`: it walks the grouped\ncatalogue and rebuilds the dotted message ids before\n`loadTranslations()` sees them.. It is made for the new english\ncatalogue in en.json because I changed the structure of it as metionned\nearlier\n\n**Documentation** — `docs/i18n-angular-usage.md`\n\n- updated for the grouped catalogue: the overview section, the folder\nmap, the worked example, the key rules, the testing notes, two new\ntroubleshooting rows, and the developer checklist\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/features/settings/pages/settings.spec.ts`\n(new): the page, its section navigation, both actions, and the\nlocalization of the template and of the snack bar message\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/app.config.spec.ts`: three unit cases for\n`flattenTranslations()`, plus one integration case that feeds the loader\na grouped catalogue and checks the English actually renders\n- `employee-frontend/src/app/app.routes.spec.ts` (new): the settings\nroute declares its guards\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n<!--\nPaste four screenshots here, in this order. Drag and drop them into the\n    GitHub form, it uploads them and inserts the markdown for you.\n\n    1. BEFORE  - /settings showing the \"Coming soon\" placeholder\n    2. AFTER   - the page in French, on the Security section\n    3. AFTER   - the page in English, to show the localization\n4. AFTER - the home page with the \"Changes saved\" snack bar visible,\n                 right after clicking Save\n\n    Keep the headings below so reviewers can tell them apart.\n-->\n\nNew UI feature: before this PR, `/settings` rendered the shared `Coming\nsoon`\nplaceholder and there was no settings UI to compare against\n\n**After — French**\n<img width=\"1890\" height=\"826\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58c038db-4e73-4fa9-89e0-19a3b4118895\"\n/>\n\n\n**After — English**\n<img width=\"1896\" height=\"831\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9fb4a97-797f-4843-b17a-c669890d0a0b\"\n/>\n\n**After — confirmation on save**\n<img width=\"1898\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f9c70016-8cf6-40b0-a960-02045a13d5e8\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwwoDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOb4QAIkYxWjyDbypdugR5NDWV6mZ\n48xdIAUYJ+JiMsxe/+CTgoDatLGSLm935Yju8Yd1qlAFmfzSDoDJohjQAFK1kf13\n6oM1VuprlHkAS/b1oaRW1wgw53q/ZFB0FIZeSzCOzBwCd6L3aVe3Gf1TXcJdiiee\nZZDCk+x0JN8etw6oGxJ2LdC9KqztnFLQd6k8LdvShKmnIGYOAv084BPqnLUnqJ8j\nOpQimbVbXjMnpRjCvCAxTVQ0ygIO4udxXcqwaOLkrnMajjLLfQA76R751PIrOZtL\nmJL8cH8vDOdNDFKbDFJoAXoCHk3OPOC4yq56+mnpZXAh/vmpv9BIKjc1q/c7QgUE\n0C7UJuDyfrToLzboKYAyxTZb/xqHzRqVspfH6aHTYp5EzXl1FEDi514jEiJD69Er\n2oEHMDelFzUc2fufMhQmBHlPSdZfH9WDOoSVkAtb9XVV/dRoMMOhk2Et4nbtNWgf\np8JCP2X/elBMCCUWosEZudFfvNL/BbC5wR7Cbposbkvh7PKEQXmTPqtTENajL5Q/\naIV9oHp+SEzU5EjvGbmVJPt0ZRSogM/0DMLtbLWe+kUd5/ayJ6c0eSe/mjRa6Knt\nmAEz0hCpncI6B/pNxT+8DudG7xLbshnz+rxveuc2XFDd7hEnzuKzrxBuq932gI29\n7sKTO6Bl7o281QcXbIxl\n=9p+i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T02:23:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"htt