rard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408"}],"sha":"f793b51e8736b5fc75e8e053a50ee9e4d061daa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f793b51e8736b5fc75e8e053a50ee9e4d061daa2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230245567?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MellonCat","id":230245567,"login":"MellonCat","node_id":"U_kgDODblEvw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:15:42Z","email":"kyle.galbraith07@gmail.com","name":"Kyle Galbraith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:15:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(BILL-CPC-1972): Filter Bypassing Filter Button (#1559)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1972)\n## Context:\nThis ticket fixes the bill filtering behavior in the Admin Bills page.\nPreviously, changing a filter value could immediately affect the\ndisplayed bills after a filter had already been applied. The expected\nbehavior is that filter changes should only be applied when the user\nclicks the **Filter** button.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Updated the bill filtering logic so filter selections are only applied\nwhen the **Filter** button is clicked.\n- Added separate applied filter state to keep the currently displayed\nfilters separate from the user''s current selections.\n- Updated status, year, and month filtering to use the applied filter\nvalues.\n- Updated the existing customer, owner, vet, and visit type filters to\nuse the applied filter values.\n- Updated the **Filter** and **Clear** buttons to close the filter modal\nafter being clicked.\n- Added an All Months option to the month filter and set it as the\ndefault selection.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThe visual design of the filter modal was not changed. The behavior was\nupdated so that:\n- Clicking **Filter** applies the selected filters and closes the modal.\n- Clicking **Clear** resets the filters and closes the modal.\n- Changing filter selections without clicking **Filter** does not change\nthe displayed bills.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe filter state is separated into draft and applied values. The draft\nvalues represent the user''s current selections in the filter modal,\nwhile the applied values represent the filters currently being used to\nfilter the bill list.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kyle Galbraith <kyleg@WHYWORLD>","tree":{"sha":"a43a82cb3987f5ae8f3e15a5d7527dc6df4f6d16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/a43a82cb3987f5ae8f3e15a5d7527dc6df4f6d16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408","verification":{"payload":"tree a43a82cb3987f5ae8f3e15a5d7527dc6df4f6d16\nparent 376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394\nauthor Kyle Galbraith <kyle.galbraith07@gmail.com> 1790910942 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790910942 -0400\n\nbug(BILL-CPC-1972): Filter Bypassing Filter Button (#1559)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1972)\n## Context:\nThis ticket fixes the bill filtering behavior in the Admin Bills page.\nPreviously, changing a filter value could immediately affect the\ndisplayed bills after a filter had already been applied. The expected\nbehavior is that filter changes should only be applied when the user\nclicks the **Filter** button.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Updated the bill filtering logic so filter selections are only applied\nwhen the **Filter** button is clicked.\n- Added separate applied filter state to keep the currently displayed\nfilters separate from the user''s current selections.\n- Updated status, year, and month filtering to use the applied filter\nvalues.\n- Updated the existing customer, owner, vet, and visit type filters to\nuse the applied filter values.\n- Updated the **Filter** and **Clear** buttons to close the filter modal\nafter being clicked.\n- Added an All Months option to the month filter and set it as the\ndefault selection.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThe visual design of the filter modal was not changed. The behavior was\nupdated so that:\n- Clicking **Filter** applies the selected filters and closes the modal.\n- Clicking **Clear** resets the filters and closes the modal.\n- Changing filter selections without clicking **Filter** does not change\nthe displayed bills.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe filter state is separated into draft and applied values. The draft\nvalues represent the user''s current selections in the filter modal,\nwhile the applied values represent the filters currently being used to\nfilter the bill list.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kyle Galbraith <kyleg@WHYWORLD>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyHeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfoIQAG9z1fH/pKBOeN3HcqAjBl7D\n3gz3++Vg/gAq6u8yyGPBK7rYpoV5HR+rzUfAp+AD66u2m1vxQB8wkad6mA66y1Sx\nXcBq3ZMqOaUKyNe54e7wQMdd8Arn7/BpVlC8FurnHWYDSnBFupXkKkavjKF3//1E\ncKgnxTAa3Wlnsw9x/KFaCxoohdfx6w1XAmJTQRgBbdX8LNieO50a+HezJetZVlA6\nVxz+PGgW4Gx2gHLKMusGvLxthRO7KuTyGTAraYAtK96om2rladb1QHCOHl9J7b18\nHOkIGBdwIqedYpj8+uhH9i5Bq6MQzBCHAzBuEvpMupa0fJ1/7x4HM/f6U5dkrthp\ngj/jYGAzOkSZdabiJV9dNmKDyGueCeoVompoLTOTA7KCdVpB9IZ+yzJnSfB7eH5P\ncUNWO6CT0BV16e8JVvybHqTnPpDZmZx/v+ElDRVD4OT7kxSLo0sCJ0Q2o6/r8vFw\nyw+LnFQtRr2Zm2ma64xxkKOb4Du9NiAPHLfJtmFHlSpFE+WCDvD6MtqX+Q5PM3Nr\nG4E+mN4f6j5aMMItkYGOeBKBAJSzZZcFpvv2NpRm1dhmpuSt5/pYf4dwK/i/GZhV\nV58x0LVUiT2cGtYipDGTBIB4BL+WWdM7mfAh/qm9L/s6jKgkriQ71G9jsMSZPvpq\nfvYb1YJv5xFpGByoh4SW\n=LP8N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T03:15:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGIzN2I1ZWI5YzZmMDIzNmJhNTQ5NjJmNDdhN2E4ZDc5ZDhkMGU0MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394","sha":"376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394"}],"sha":"b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/b37b5eb9c6f0236ba54962f47a7a8d79d8d0e408"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167457702?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ELS20680","id":167457702,"login":"ELS20680","node_id":"U_kgDOCfszpg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELS20680","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:08:56Z","email":"167457702+ELS20680@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ELS20680"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:08:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(BILL-CPC-1989): return 404 for missing bill pdf (#1561)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[BILL-CPC-1989](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1989)\n## Context:\nThis ticket is about returning the correct response when someone tries\nto download a PDF for a bill that does not exist.\nBefore this change, the billing service returned a 500 Internal Server\nError. Since the bill cannot be found, it should return 404 Not Found.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not change the .vscode folder or any frontend files.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Changed missing bills to use NotFoundException.\n- Updated the staff and customer PDF endpoints to return 404 Not Found\nwhen the bill does not exist.\n- Kept unexpected PDF-generation errors returning 500 Internal Server\nError.\n- Added tests for missing staff and customer bill PDFs.\n- Changes only affect the billing-service module.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. This PR does not use or change the v2 API.\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This PR does not add any new communication between services, so the\nC4 L2 diagram does not need to be updated.\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNot applicable because this is a backend-only change and does not affect\nthe UI.","tree":{"sha":"1a5b65f3ed9f68fb3dd8967f65a529cd754f4e6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/1a5b65f3ed9f68fb3dd8967f65a529cd754f4e6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/376f3de115a0d47bf347d68f5cb81fd6e5503394","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a5b65f3ed9f68fb3dd8967f65a529cd754f4e6c\nparent fe6f3fc6775c3f312f44484942cc1e5529d28ef6\nauthor ELS20680 <167457702+ELS20680@users.noreply.github.com> 1790910536 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790910536 -0400\n\nfix(BILL-CPC-1989): return 404 for missing bill pdf (#1561)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[BILL-CPC-1989](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1989)\n## Context:\nThis ticket is about returning the correct response when someone tries\nto download a PDF for a bill that does not exist.\nBefore this change, the billing service returned a 500 Internal Server\nError. Since the bill cannot be found, it should return 404 Not Found.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not change the .vscode folder or any frontend files.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Changed missing bills to use NotFoundException.\n- Updated the staff and customer PDF endpoints to return 404 Not Found\nwhen the bill does not exist.\n- Kept unexpected PDF-generation errors returning 500 Internal Server\nError.\n- Added tests for missing staff and customer bill PDFs.\n- Changes only affect the billing-service module.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. This PR does not use or change the v2 API.\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This PR does not add any new communication b