y are we doing this change.\n\nadmins had no way of updating, deleting and editing promotions without\nmaking a manual sql query to the db.\n\nthere was a react promo dashboard in the current customer frontend if\nyou logged in with the admin account but it failed to fetch the promos\nand editing them\n\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\nN/A\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\nN/A \n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n\n- added a promo management page to the angular employee app (list,\nadd/edit modal, delete, active/inactive toggle)\n- added an active flag to the promo request in cart-service and\napi-gateway so the toggle saves\n- deactivated promos now show as inactive and fail checkout validation\n- fixed gateway promo list call (asks for event-stream, was getting\na 406)\n- cart-service promo id check now accepts 24-char (seeded) and 36-char\nids\n- react: fixed add promo trailing slash and made delete refresh the list\n- react customer and admin promo pages kept as they were\n- added tests for promos\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why\n\nyes, the promo endpoints only exist in the v2 gateway\n(_/api/v2/gateway/promos_), and the react promo pages already used v2.\n\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nN/A\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\n\n**before**\n\n<img width=\"1143\" height=\"305\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6227472-7864-43c8-8e26-ee9c172aa090\"\n/>\n\n\n\n**after**\n\n<img width=\"1905\" height=\"616\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8624c2c3-c7d0-4ad4-8222-177d08b920ad\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1364\" height=\"665\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c9df04b-dbd6-4a28-bd5f-255816d7d697\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1417\" height=\"735\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0732c51f-3984-4fad-83a2-9371687084e7\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1750\" height=\"550\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/686ef9fc-a418-41c2-91b0-2247598e8faf\"\n/>\n\n\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show reviewers what\nit looks like.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yanis Achamou <yanisachamou@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdff5808f473eba501bca79c45fe5802e7ad6dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/bdff5808f473eba501bca79c45fe5802e7ad6dab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/2e92d95561bb608a250a60dd6313a6e2c0d961c4","verification":{"payload":"tree bdff5808f473eba501bca79c45fe5802e7ad6dab\nparent 84e99a332d643d700bd335402fc688098e167e23\nauthor Youcef <youcef68001@gmail.com> 1790907558 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790907558 -0400\n\nbug(CART-CPC-1879): promo dashboard for employee frontend + fix for react frontend (#1565)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1879\n## Context:\nWhat is the ticket about and why are we doing this change.\n\nadmins had no way of updating, deleting and editing promotions without\nmaking a manual sql query to the db.\n\nthere was a react promo dashboard in the current customer frontend if\nyou logged in with the admin account but it failed to fetch the promos\nand editing them\n\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\nN/A\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\nN/A \n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n\n- added a promo management page to the angular employee app (list,\nadd/edit modal, delete, active/inactive toggle)\n- added an active flag to the promo request in cart-service and\napi-gateway so the toggle saves\n- deactivated promos now show as inactive and fail checkout validation\n- fixed gateway promo list call (asks for event-stream, was getting\na 406)\n- cart-service promo id check now accepts 24-char (seeded) and 36-char\nids\n- react: fixed add promo trailing slash and made delete refresh the list\n- react customer and admin promo pages kept as they were\n- added tests for promos\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why\n\nyes, the promo endpoints only exist in the v2 gateway\n(_/api/v2/gateway/promos_), and the react promo pages already used v2.\n\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nN/A\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\n\n**before**\n\n<img width=\"1143\" height=\"305\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6227472-7864-43c8-8e26-ee9c172aa090\"\n/>\n\n\n\n**after**\n\n<img width=\"1905\" height=\"616\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8624c2c3-c7d0-4ad4-8222-177d08b920ad\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1364\" height=\"665\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c9df04b-dbd6-4a28-bd5f-255816d7d697\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1417\" height=\"735\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0732c51f-3984-4fad-83a2-9371687084e7\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1750\" height=\"550\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/686ef9fc-a418-41c2-91b0-2247598e8faf\"\n/>\n\n\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show reviewers what\nit looks like.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yanis Achamou <yanisachamou@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvxSmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYbYQAGwGsMJlsHPjemgypsgzDE3R\nrhihodMbh3aeTH/NcaGraXcBC5DAy/0URJyayrcCceOZrC1apJrxqLQwtdW0Dx4m\nmqvgbZ+Px58eWrjCGmHsAR+TvrwhIGd2LbHHBrmiG1sOsKrXFAabxQ/gE1TaoJ9O\nAWq95p2kIS9b9TfT/lZVUDRAURlgJz8t6ffCf10pwhaWWzZj2MPyW7Alh6HatpGE\n9M7RJ1XskPhWX35j+FfME2JPMWkT1+C7DBUQke/gUwp7XIrIV1bfTCu7voYedlfk\nvZA9h3FESFYnqYNOQ+WhT9mDkl802GE7oHb6Yeb2Oj2n9jFU8jbXzdciqLO69Nsk\n9SB6gb9bmmQJ1y135iR2OivLrbOzmMB8xnVLVapCnjuEOtX2FmNqcbeaiJ2MHuNR\nlqIM/433xkWgujGktozQHKHAlJd8BCUpYUZhjVP2BZLwXeVwrClr+OJXz0Z4neL2\nz0u5k3ldekaaoaUMA0F/6NDv7eO530cMPd4DmOhBH0I/PqdzJ0fA+5oRWXJPhdJZ\ng8SLAIQZ4HS+OldDqzjXyHfREPqneE4FyJ4oGKoda7eGsG7uCM0oLejYZZcmT6Kg\nHE9QeEhNUp5JswTK/H91IU9jV0PJXobzLpprPhLHMZkyhw6DTaW/VKVX7lX+fDbQ\nI/7Eelcac1SWdFo2XSuW\n=9B0P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T02:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/we