kwDOF4d909oAKDg0ZTk5YTMzMmQ2NDNkNzAwYmQzMzU0MDJmYzY4ODA5OGUxNjdlMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318","sha":"5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318"}],"sha":"84e99a332d643d700bd335402fc688098e167e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/84e99a332d643d700bd335402fc688098e167e23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190027213?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Eric909090","id":190027213,"login":"Eric909090","node_id":"U_kgDOC1OVzQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eric909090","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:09:11Z","email":"ionascueric0@gmail.com","name":"Eric Ionascu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:09:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(VIST-CPC-1751): Update frontend handling of reactive streams (#1522)\n\n**JIRA:** CPC-1751\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/70?selectedIssue=CPC-1751\n## Context:\nThe Visit customer FE had 2 issues:  \n- The data stream was all loaded at once   \n- The splitting and filtering (happening in the FE) broke the reactive\nstream\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nTo solve the issues I:   \n- Reworked the filtering of streams   \n- Made so the loading of the streams load as they arrive (async) instead\nof waiting for them to all arrive and load them all at once\n- Added so when a user leaves the page it cancels the http request   \n- Added a readssestream.ts file (comments were added to the code to help\nunderstand how it works)\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIt uses v1\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNo changes to the UI. Only change is the React FE now loads streams as\nthey arrive (more noticable with bad wifi)\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe React visit pages now receive visit data incrementally through\nServer-Sent Events instead of waiting for the complete response. The\nstream reader uses Axios. Each complete SSE event is buffered and parsed\nbefore being sent to the UI, so visits appear as they arrive.\nI decided to change getVets.ts since AddingVisit, EditingVisit,\nOwnerAddingVisit, OwnerBookingVisit expect a VetResponseModel but my\ngetVet return a VetResponse instead causing an application crash. Using\nthe already implemented model is also a cleaner code approach\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Luis Rodriguez <luisenrique30qc@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a54c58a88a41ae8903b104044e0970649e70905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/0a54c58a88a41ae8903b104044e0970649e70905"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a54c58a88a41ae8903b104044e0970649e70905\nparent 10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3\nauthor Eric Ionascu <ionascueric0@gmail.com> 1790906951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790906951 -0400\n\nbug(VIST-CPC-1751): Update frontend handling of reactive streams (#1522)\n\n**JIRA:** CPC-1751\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/70?selectedIssue=CPC-1751\n## Context:\nThe Visit customer FE had 2 issues:  \n- The data stream was all loaded at once   \n- The splitting and filtering (happening in the FE) broke the reactive\nstream\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nTo solve the issues I:   \n- Reworked the filtering of streams   \n- Made so the loading of the streams load as they arrive (async) instead\nof waiting for them to all arrive and load them all at once\n- Added so when a user leaves the page it cancels the http request   \n- Added a readssestream.ts file (comments were added to the code to help\nunderstand how it works)\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIt uses v1\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNo changes to the UI. Only change is the React FE now loads streams as\nthey arrive (more noticable with bad wifi)\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe React visit pages now receive visit data incrementally through\nServer-Sent Events instead of waiting for the complete response. The\nstream reader uses Axios. Each complete SSE event is buffered and parsed\nbefore being sent to the UI, so visits appear as they arrive.\nI decided to change getVets.ts since AddingVisit, EditingVisit,\nOwnerAddingVisit, OwnerBookingVisit expect a VetResponseModel but my\ngetVet return a VetResponse instead causing an application crash. Using\nthe already implemented model is also a cleaner code approach\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Luis Rodriguez <luisenrique30qc@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvxJHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd9IQABPstWEhxe5khmInOMqTvwIj\nG09wxnPaYDohJWUwo3fMtajpE3aW1qxXp7+deRUti+NIYqYFq1TMbzbGJHR1McvZ\ntbAdR9Hhk4T4ABOt3KKkaYlLVicpGdH5F7vCb2Y2aMsaGCwsoVMsAW96K0roQF8D\nbK4X3KhlO60ykrXC37IolL3w5WJIxP/ZT2N9QAH8q2tSlU6gRDEiPqzhigRaN7jq\nTgmO9zp5ccj+k6dU47j+fs5xyOpI5plgBnxGVKiZunNKnTkn2u9Xom82VL03UiaM\nd0WLd7cqHZ+VHYU/LLKZ5uFmcGONsV8i9xM+dYuStylE0zXM0afD28N98qNKvwpJ\nQwNVfhVFXCEkwfAt4Dk4WIKRV8S8v1JzkD1eww9cVNk+sQTOZAHqcDtx4dKfA7Dv\n/nW7O6ZrX+9ji3m+mHuImYjithYbPUe0g0WESz8IEKdKvVVEwa/0jWOeQiHXUyCO\nzH1IG1sJcd2DpxubZkdPg7Cl7tlY1f/x18o36SldAlyyAHu3/1oNNzmPso1a4ZLC\nq1LgzRpLVLT3YWtxBYG/t+rEUTXYAZ+in3nT7vGi41+8EFbDjAnZX2hroPQ12Eaj\no4eoEmyZyt3FlM62S/eCoSY7lN5zue1fIEZQ46d/URfX6a9wHSCzFwwgPo4/hXpQ\nNdjYpX/1kuSqnaUkac+s\n=KxYY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T02:09:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDU1ODlmMDUxNTNiNDI4YmRmMGExODc0NmM0ZDRjNGM5YzE4OGUzMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3","sha":"10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3"}],"sha":"5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/5589f05153b428bdf0a18746c4d4c4c9c188e318"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203462650?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/iba213","id":203462650,"login":"iba213","node_id":"U_kgDODCCX-g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iba213","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T01:55:45Z","email":"eliasibaliden@gmail.com","name":"Elias Ibaliden"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T01:55:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VETS-CPC-1978): add veterinarians placeholder page (#1523)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1978\n\n## Context\nAdds the starting Veterinarians landing page for the Angular Employee\nPortal, with a responsive design and placeholders for future features.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Organizes the page under features/vets/pages/veterinarians.\n- Updates the vets feature route and replaces the temporary placeholder.\n- Uses the existing Veterinarians navigation link.\n- Adds a directory panel with clearly labelled sample profile initials.\n- Adds Working hours and Specialties cards marked “Coming soon.”\n- Keeps Explore directory disabled until the directory is implemented.\n- Adds responsive styling and hover effects that respect reduced-motion\npreferences.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\nNo. No API calls were added. No real veterinarian data is displayed.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI\nBefore: the temporary page displayed \"Vets Works!\"\n<img width=\"1243\" height=\"421\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fd46b0e-dcfc-4abd-bae0-1432ea9757c4\"\n/>\n\n\nAfter: /vets displays a styled Veterinarians landing page with a\ndirectory panel and two future-feature cards.\n<img width=\"1992\" height=\"881\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a754ab84-984d-4198-8396-8904747819dd\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes\n- Production build passed with an Inventory CSS budget warning.\n- Automated tests were blocked during compilation by TS2532 in\n  features/inventories/routes.spec.ts:7.\n- The directory page, schedules, specialties functionality, and backend\nintegration are outside this PR’s scope.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elias Ibaliden <elias@DESKTOP-926F9T3>","tree":{"sha":"910e421de756333b6a97f3881b98229be0ede4da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/910e421de756333b6a97f3881b98229be0ede4da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3","verification":{"payload":"tree 910e421de756333b6a97f3881b98229be0ede4da\nparent e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e\nauthor Elias Ibaliden <eliasibaliden@gmail.com> 1790906145 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790906145 -0400\n\nfeat(VETS-CPC-1978): add veterinarians placeholder page (#1523)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1978\n\n## Context\nAdds the starting Veterinarians landing page for the Angular Employee\nPortal, with a responsive design and placeholders for future features.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Organizes the page under features/vets/pages/veterinarians.\n- Updates the vets feature route and replaces the temporary placeholder.\n- Uses the existing Veterinarians navigation link.\n- Adds a directory panel with clearly labelled sample profile initials.\n- Adds Working hours and Specialties cards marked “Coming soon.”\n- Keeps Explore directory disabled until the directory is implemented.\n- Adds responsive styling and hover effects that respect reduced-motion\npreferences.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\nNo. No API calls were added. No real veterinarian data is displayed.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI\nBefore: the temporary page displayed \"Vets Works!\"\n<img width=\"1243\" height=\"421\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fd46b0e-dcfc-4abd-bae0-1432ea9757c4\"\n/>\n\n\nAfter: /vets displays a styled Veterinarians landing page with a\ndirectory panel and two future-feature cards.\n<img width=\"1992\" height=\"881\" alt=\