ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDEwNzQ0ZTMzMjVlM2FhNjg1MTU2ZmMxOGFkYWRiMDU4ZmQzNGNiYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e","sha":"e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e"}],"sha":"10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/10744e3325e3aa685156fc18adadb058fd34cba3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180322279?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ilianadeleke","id":180322279,"login":"ilianadeleke","node_id":"U_kgDOCr9_5w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T00:40:26Z","email":"iladelek@gmail.com","name":"IlianLawson_DEV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T00:40:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":" feat(CUST-CPC-2037)-fix-failing-customers-reactive-test (#1556)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2037?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNTY1MjRlNDRjZmVhNGE1MmE4OTc5MDlmYzM1YWYzMmMiLCJwIjoiaiJ9)\n## Context:\nThe ticket reported a recurring but also inconcistent bug in the build\nthat kept failing because of a delete test in the\nCustomerControllerIntegrationTest. Sometimes it was fixed and sometime\nit was not working anymore, I tried to mitigate the issue by conforming\nthe test and the endpoint to the Rest principle (delete should return\n204 not 200)\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n**No.** This PR only affects the `customers-service-reactive` backend\nmicroservice. No changes are made to the frontend or `.vscode`\nconfiguration.\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n**No.** This PR maintains compatibility with the existing API structure.\nIt only changes HTTP status codes for DELETE operations, not the API\nversion or endpoints themselves.\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n**No.** This PR does not add new inter-service communication. It only\nrefactors HTTP response codes for existing DELETE endpoints.\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThere was no effect on the UI.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n**Technical Changes**\n\n- REST Semantic Alignment: DELETE operations now correctly return 204 No\nContent, indicating successful deletion with no content to return.\n- Response Type Change: Changed from ResponseEntity<CustomerResponseDTO>\nto ResponseEntity<Void> to signal that no body is returned.\n- Change for Clients: Frontend/API consumers must update code to handle\n204 status (no JSON response body to parse).","tree":{"sha":"6007bcf20383904a60dbc8555f4d1da2f10cb585","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/6007bcf20383904a60dbc8555f4d1da2f10cb585"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e","verification":{"payload":"tree 6007bcf20383904a60dbc8555f4d1da2f10cb585\nparent 837722e44e8d8bec8ad3b46b678ec9f65ec9c158\nauthor IlianLawson_DEV <iladelek@gmail.com> 1790901626 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790901626 -0400\n\n feat(CUST-CPC-2037)-fix-failing-customers-reactive-test (#1556)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2037?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNTY1MjRlNDRjZmVhNGE1MmE4OTc5MDlmYzM1YWYzMmMiLCJwIjoiaiJ9)\n## Context:\nThe ticket reported a recurring but also inconcistent bug in the build\nthat kept failing because of a delete test in the\nCustomerControllerIntegrationTest. Sometimes it was fixed and sometime\nit was not working anymore, I tried to mitigate the issue by conforming\nthe test and the endpoint to the Rest principle (delete should return\n204 not 200)\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n**No.** This PR only affects the `customers-service-reactive` backend\nmicroservice. No changes are made to the frontend or `.vscode`\nconfiguration.\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n**No.** This PR maintains compatibility with the existing API structure.\nIt only changes HTTP status codes for DELETE operations, not the API\nversion or endpoints themselves.\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n**No.** This PR does not add new inter-service communication. It only\nrefactors HTTP response codes for existing DELETE endpoints.\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThere was no effect on the UI.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n**Technical Changes**\n\n- REST Semantic Alignment: DELETE operations now correctly return 204 No\nContent, indicating successful deletion with no content to return.\n- Response Type Change: Changed from ResponseEntity<CustomerResponseDTO>\nto ResponseEntity<Void> to signal that no body is returned.\n- Change for Clients: Frontend/API consumers must update code to handle\n204 status (no JSON response body to parse).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvv16CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZtkQAGbUQApW0xt/vqI6gS9xTnh0\n/E2OkdxgqzYu93x+nL11siKQ/tHtG+kR7F8zojv9CP9AWMMwqhHeZLRoXdG/VeyT\n4p6BzczXznz6yGqhUtKqyQjIAmNP/kz0VUdHNMFwBvYrSCHhvo6IsHfgW2sa7Ixe\n12qiHwnN/wfuBhJYh4OZpuYjlg7OfLxFP4/HXaMb/tDxb+7Xe8odOVmA9oB/WBV+\nF3CuWRzgswVWGJY1Mrd22iV+tV4671TM4CDY8xbdMzOT3xHA8OEsiExjZIC1Rgm0\nQfmYPM59dcwV5R4kpk0NI539LWf9TNnnOdwaQegScaZfXvnjPRiYOWwv3B1idCto\nXi7r4TH1MyewVFvtMbM4H/kY1pVinSm6Pxuw5chy2ghijUjj6gY6GA8eyLXeoiHJ\nMd/1rfZ7YyjuKCSN7vJYN0Hd+EBHb248Qg1mHXPjjqyotu3VR1BLlFDZEONSRji2\nRg2S7Dp8jIqtu3iVbQlkVpCCnThmB4YgOZnZ6w5qFvxYKBnxy7YDrte0wowcxdJ8\nx5qNGHMFDzTlWH0imek38D7kEL6MOoEG0oJST5v5lYyqhPr37/tnlXVGKBS06bkp\nLILoWde13AVaUisa4sBN1NtkCRllQrVX1AGqAbRXyzXj9bycai5Cf8fb7XpRuTJO\nley/ee8CpMmrP7xwpLLa\n=AH35\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T00:40:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGUzMDBjZWM2YjNlYmI5ZjVjMGU2YWEzYzI3MzhmZWNiZTgzYWE2OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/837722e44e8d8bec8ad3b46b678ec9f65ec9c158","sha":"837722e44e8d8bec8ad3b46b678ec9f65ec9c158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/837722e44e8d8bec8ad3b46b678ec9f65ec9c158"}],"sha":"e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e300cec6b3ebb9f5c0e6aa3c2738fecbe83aa69e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103219890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/williammarcotte","id":103219890,"login":"williammarcotte","node_id":"U_kgDOBicCsg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williammarcotte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/837722e44e8d8bec8ad3b46b678ec9f65ec9c158/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:51:56Z","email":"103219890+williammarcotte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"williammarcotte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:51:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug/(VIST-CPC-1955) delete cancelled visits returns 404 when none exist (#1549)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1955\n## Context:\nCurrently, when calling Delete /visits/cancelled returns 204 No Content\neven when there are no cancelled visits to delete.\nThe endpoint should return 404 Not Found when no cancelled visits exist.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n## Changes\n- Updated deleteAllCancelledVisits() in VisitServiceImpl to throw a\nNotFoundException when no cancelled visits are found.\n- Updated VisitServiceImplTest to cover the new behavior.\n- Updated deleteAllCancelledVisits in VisitsController to use\nthenReturn() instead of map(), as there is no value emitted.\n- Updated VisitsServiceClient to throw NotFoundException on a \n404 Not Found response\n- Updated VisitControllerUnitTest to reflect new behavior\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNo changes to UI.\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show reviewers what\nit looks like.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nNo notes.\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNo requests.","tree":{"sha":"890e99f26265888bf8bd81f982c98aa8b858a3a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/890e99f26265888bf8bd81f982c98aa8b858a3a9"},"url"