cc570f42dfc06dc31c88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230245843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MrLerc","id":230245843,"login":"MrLerc","node_id":"U_kgDODblF0w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrLerc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f5baebfcdf2aaecb95ed081b42237f4b947504c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:12:31Z","email":"luisenrique30qc@gmail.com","name":"Luis Rodriguez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:12:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(VIST-CPC-1954): Fix VIST-CPC-1954 - Past appointments are displayed with an Upcoming status (#1504)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1954\n\n## Context:\n\nWhat is the ticket about and why are we doing this change.\n\nPast appointments were being displayed with an UPCOMING status even\nthough their appointment end date had already passed. This change\nensures that expired appointments are no longer treated as upcoming and\nthat their status is updated to COMPLETED.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\n\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\n## Changes\n\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\n\n* Updated the Visits service to detect UPCOMING visits whose end date\nhas already passed.\n* Changed expired UPCOMING visits to COMPLETED and saved the updated\nstatus.\n* Updated the default Visit seed data so past appointments are not\ncreated with an UPCOMING status.\n* Preserved existing CANCELLED and ARCHIVED statuses.\n* Changes affect the `visits-service-new` module.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why.\n\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show what it looks\nlike.\n\nNot applicable. This PR does not make changes to the UI. The change is\nimplemented in the Visits backend service.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted.\n\nThe Visits status filtering now checks stored UPCOMING visits against\ntheir `visitEndDate`. If the end date has passed, the visit is updated\nto COMPLETED before the requested status results are returned.\n\nTesting:\n\n.\\gradlew.bat :visits-service:test\n\nResult: BUILD SUCCESSFUL\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\nPull request links.\n\nNone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Noah Bouffard <noahbouff@hotmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad5dfcd1e6f32e7bd1bfe89592257fa7c35a33de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/ad5dfcd1e6f32e7bd1bfe89592257fa7c35a33de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/f5baebfcdf2aaecb95ed081b42237f4b947504c6","verification":{"payload":"tree ad5dfcd1e6f32e7bd1bfe89592257fa7c35a33de\nparent 77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191\nauthor Luis Rodriguez <luisenrique30qc@gmail.com> 1790881951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790881951 -0400\n\nbug(VIST-CPC-1954): Fix VIST-CPC-1954 - Past appointments are displayed with an Upcoming status (#1504)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1954\n\n## Context:\n\nWhat is the ticket about and why are we doing this change.\n\nPast appointments were being displayed with an UPCOMING status even\nthough their appointment end date had already passed. This change\nensures that expired appointments are no longer treated as upcoming and\nthat their status is updated to COMPLETED.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\n\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\n## Changes\n\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\n\n* Updated the Visits service to detect UPCOMING visits whose end date\nhas already passed.\n* Changed expired UPCOMING visits to COMPLETED and saved the updated\nstatus.\n* Updated the default Visit seed data so past appointments are not\ncreated with an UPCOMING status.\n* Preserved existing CANCELLED and ARCHIVED statuses.\n* Changes affect the `visits-service-new` module.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why.\n\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show what it looks\nlike.\n\nNot applicable. This PR does not make changes to the UI. The change is\nimplemented in the Visits backend service.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted.\n\nThe Visits status filtering now checks stored UPCOMING visits against\ntheir `visitEndDate`. If the end date has passed, the visit is updated\nto COMPLETED before the requested status results are returned.\n\nTesting:\n\n.\\gradlew.bat :visits-service:test\n\nResult: BUILD SUCCESSFUL\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\nPull request links.\n\nNone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Noah Bouffard <noahbouff@hotmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvrCfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5CUQAAQzKR1AL/qkuyXmSV2lgXDm\nT9rnRv6E9BkOF+OWzWO2FzWGwJcHrGdPMvxrJXmCi12FU1H+cznwcKq2bTlrRiiA\nvQV3bvj4WAaI4k2d4Rfwk9GamNWjf4nDxqWfRLrEOzeORud3EKBMYqxHN91ZC6Oq\noUHp/DeLThlzTSw5qFosIOFFAfy9Aox7t2aWNnYCD6TdvpBi0vLSp5m61/QFs+lT\nPMAFdubT+L+01TQGMgmKw1GlP8FIqUhkoxUiWypud4yCokJqTLBiauE/JU5xI41p\nyVSuUtLJv8SXgyvmxGzeeGhwBqWCOuFkpWceIYBYAzrn/AXx7Rub65aAC2iscZBe\nyybFmBYeI/NBhy3LeY1aWa/zYb1RurSJt3wMTcRlne26z07AAwIiG8bCJzx79NlL\nMcW5g0+VVZ7RizV2c/Ij/mtNRLPLGCZq5pVkAbowPWtNXfH+UDOpAewe6hL4KaAk\n7Ygghb591m4qeU1XtWMV67GlFcicCwI7wvcs69RXHTOQhVEa61acF/1z0jKYf3rR\nOIGZnJFH1nHevZjNn8xGGeQ1tzkvSSCgpT084Lypebl5rv1X9P+V1mozQvhBoUan\n6/4UXnOKAxfoBeL8VPVv1FpjepPQwMX53PhbYxG4RqHOTWwr/3NegcFRDZ9vQ/S2\nrximMU2ZA6POs4WQRNUV\n=cviq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T19:12:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/f5baebfcdf2aaecb95ed081b42237f4b947504c6","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGY1YmFlYmZjZGYyYWFlY2I5NWVkMDgxYjQyMjM3ZjRiOTQ3NTA0YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191","sha":"77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191"}],"sha":"f5baebfcdf2aaecb95ed081b42237f4b947504c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f5baebfcdf2aaecb95ed081b42237f4b947504c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63722895?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rami38","id":63722895,"login":"Rami38","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzIyODk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:40:33Z","email":"63722895+Rami38@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Yacoub Bakayoko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:40:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-1970): Localize CustomerDetails, UpdateCustomerForm, AdminUpdateCustomerForm (#1551)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1970\n\n## Context:\nThe customer profile views and forms only showed English text. This\nlocalizes CustomerDetails, UpdateCustomerForm and\nAdminUpdateCustomerForm so all their text switches between English and\nFrench with the LanguageSwitcher, using the i18n setup from CPC-1962.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n## Changes\n- Added keys to public/locales/en/customers.json and fr/customers.json:\nshared `fields` labels, `customerDetails`, `customerForm`, `validation`\n- CustomerDetails: headings, labels, buttons, empty states,\nconfirm/alert messages and img alt text use t(). Pet age uses i18next\nplurals (1 year / 2 years, 1 an / 2 ans)\n- UpdateCustomerForm and AdminUpdateCustomerForm: labels, title,\nbuttons, toasts, success modal and validation messages use t()\n- utils/validation.ts: returns translation keys instead of English\nsentences; the forms translate them when rendering, so errors already on\nscreen change language when switching\n- Only used by these two forms, so no other component is affected\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n<img width=\"1852\" height=\"1102\"\nalt=\"cpc-1970-before-customer-edit-profile-form\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b83242d-d2d1-43d1-8063-dbf3b6ae8994\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1850\" height=\"1081\" alt=\"cpc-1970-before-customer-edit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e870d055-f3bc-4f46-9a5a-d2b99733e4fb\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1855\" height=\"1096\" alt=\"cpc-1970-bedore-customer-details\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bfc65a9b-3495-4845-9454-f95af4511392\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1842\" height=\"1075\"\nalt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-edit-profile-form\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac3517ca-a9d5-4792-96e2-befab595992c\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1841\" height=\"1092\" alt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-edit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26a0be9a-1392-42a2-b8c7-6131e71ee4fb\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1837\" height=\"1087\" alt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-details\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2443738a-277f-4c42-9b4d-a003253219c2\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- AddPetModal / EditPetModal are not part of this ticket and stay in\nEnglish\n- AdminUpdateCustomerForm keeps its existing telephone rule (digits\nonly); no validation rules were changed\n\nCo-authored-by: Yacoub Bakayoko <2431671@champlaincollege.qc.ca>","tree":{"sha":"72fbd03094f58c21751e149a094236fa6a247a44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/72fbd03094f58c21751e149a094236fa6a247a44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191","verification":{"payload":"tree 72fbd03094f58c21751e149a094236fa6a247a44\nparent fbd110ad44fb9494be54ea2003810358a6777946\nauthor Yacoub Bakayoko <63722895+Rami38@users.noreply.github.com> 1790880033 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790880033 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-1970): Localize CustomerDetails, UpdateCustomerForm, AdminUpdateCustomerForm (#1551)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1970\n\n## Context:\nThe customer profile views and forms only showed English text. This\nlocalizes CustomerDetails, UpdateCustomerForm and\nAdminUpdateCustomerForm so all their text switches between English and\nFrench with the LanguageSwitcher, using the i18n setup from CPC-1962.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n## Changes\n- Added keys to public/locales/en/customers.json and fr/customers.json:\nshared `fields` labels, `customerDetails`, `customerForm`, `validation`\n- CustomerDetails: headings, labels, buttons, empty states,\nconfirm/alert messages and img alt text use t(). Pet age uses i18next\nplurals (1 year / 2 years, 1 an / 2 ans)\n- UpdateCustomerForm and AdminUpdateCustomerForm: labels, title,\nbuttons, toasts, success modal and validation messages use t()\n- utils/validation.ts: returns translation keys instead of English\nsentences; the forms translate them when rendering, so errors already on\nscreen change language when switching\n- Only used by these two forms, so no other component is affected\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n<img width=\"1852\" height=\"1102\"\nalt=\"cpc-1970-before-customer-edit-profile-form\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b83242d-d2d1-43d1-8063-dbf3b6ae8994\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1850\" height=\"1081\" alt=\"cpc-1970-before-customer-edit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e870d055-f3bc-4f46-9a5a-d2b99733e4fb\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1855\" height=\"1096\" alt=\"cpc-1970-bedore-customer-details\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bfc65a9b-3495-4845-9454-f95af4511392\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1842\" height=\"1075\"\nalt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-edit-profile-form\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac3517ca-a9d5-4792-96e2-befab595992c\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1841\" height=\"1092\" alt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-edit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26a0be9a-1392-42a2-b8c7-6131e71ee4fb\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1837\" height=\"1087\" alt=\"cpc-1970-after-customer-details\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2443738a-277f-4c42-9b4d-a003253219c2\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- AddPetModal / EditPetModal are not part of this ticket and stay in\nEnglish\n- AdminUpdateCustomerForm keeps its existing telephone rule (digits\nonly); no validation rules were changed\n\nCo-authored-by: Yacoub Bakayoko <2431671@champlaincollege.qc.ca>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvqkhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc7kQAIF+x5sks7XitT8Nfg00ftgN\n2C4Duu3UqbwQRsgqzMfzkUroDQlWGwnjbHMqF+oThHzm5Jl4CSXnhdsgc+4ZXPZn\nqMqNGrc7+KqdVmTxIMK0g0mRsVw9LwpZfae5ASsmoXzTSBB8Dru5TcQWHB8i8Y0N\n09YzQILUK4OKbtkIH7PqTEPq04Mgj69rl19w+vWFaRGE1uq7pjqkYa7k0OIPiYgh\nYSUT+oHpbbltFaiEAedtkW9JKjcNcRpGDR5l4K8+omAQ1e1JVf/4eLcpRck2YK3a\nw/94zoBYVOPXIrTPIL/iskbtM6WRodiENS2pybWUn9fEhiy3EgaqcmoKbwu309kq\nHqicVz1CNwhiTvvo1jsq6Ci5hJfqCPH9fB1R+cuWWoijdMzH2dMqqzVJjxm/OjxD\npVmLCwI9vRlpjxoJoxr280kNY7a/FUIlxVqJAAmXiPNZkQMweaC8yk/A9XbUmC2Y\nMXCgWLH8P+3d8aWqZYRhWUifIiYw60bvJTYVO0kdq1tsMMnhVbI+6yTSI7Mfsmmk\ntp4uVd5gEnP3vtEu72CiX+1MXiJ0iOmQxJyqGNQfF5Atj3FCBx4vJ+JVpOpR+TlH\nwXj0e0o+oYoxK61GSsNlHmDWCsIb1z0GWaR/JIsMSTSnZ0muOYOwNBafSiZzOMDN\n/qR1rkWGLqTd0XviFsTm\n=5vS7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T18:40:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDc3ZmMwZWIxNTJiYWIyZjQ3MDFlYjE5ZDdkYjA3M2U5MjI1ZWYxOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/fbd110ad44fb9494be54ea2003810358a6777946","sha":"fbd110ad44fb9494be54ea2003810358a6777946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/fbd110ad44fb9494be54ea2003810358a6777946"}],"sha":"77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/77fc0eb152bab2f4701eb19d7db073e9225ef191"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193664859?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LKBSM","id":193664859,"login":"LKBSM","node_id":"U_kgDOC4sXWw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LKBSM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/fbd110ad44fb9494be54ea2003810358a6777946/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:08:04Z","email":"loukmanebessam@gmail.com","name":"LKBSM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:08:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VETS-CPC-1927): internationalization of employee frontend (#1485)\n\n**JIRA:** link to jira ticket\n\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/14?selectedIssue=CPC-1927\n\n## Context:\nThis ticket sets up internationalization for the employee portal so the\ninterface can be used in French or English. French is the source\nlanguage, written directly in the templates, and English is loaded at\nruntime from a catalogue. It also adds the FR/EN switcher, a footer, and\ntranslates the login page.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Installed and configured `@angular/localize`, the official Angular\ni18n package, with French as the source locale (`angular.json`).\n- Added the FR and EN buttons to the header. The choice is saved in\n`localStorage` and the page reloads to apply it.\n- Created the footer, which did not exist in the current `layout/`\nstructure, and translated it.\n- Translated the login page.\n- Added the English catalogue in `public/i18n/en.json`, including keys\nprepared for the forbidden and not-found pages that are still empty\nstubs owned by CPC-1981.\n- Added 15 unit tests: the footer and login page in both languages, the\nswitcher, and the loader with its two failure paths.\n- Added `docs/i18n-angular-usage.md`, linked from the README, explaining\nhow to translate a new component.\n- Fixed one line in `features/inventories/routes.spec.ts` which blocked\nthe whole test suite from compiling.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo, this PR does not call any API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, only frontend changes.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nBefore, no switcher and no footer, the interface only in English:\n\nAfter, FR and EN buttons in the header and a translated footer, French\nby default:\n\n**Login page, French (default):**\n\n<img width=\"1568\" height=\"675\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/154f43cb-374b-439a-89ea-d88165b9d91c\"\n/>\n\n**Login page, English:**\n\n<img width=\"1568\" height=\"675\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cd1eeab-68ba-4df8-abea-7deb32108b93\"\n/>\n\n**Home page, French (default):**\n\n<img width=\"1916\" height=\"821\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6ae1eba-805b-4555-aece-e4488ef1062e\"\n/>\n\n**Home page, English (after selecting EN in the header):**\n\n<img width=\"1876\" height=\"825\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1e467a5-6cb7-4af1-93ce-747e546f55e2\"\n/>\n\n> **Note on the English login screenshot:** the login page has no\nswitcher of its own, since the switcher lives in the header and the\nheader is inside the shell, behind the auth guard. English is reached by\nselecting EN from the header while signed in: the choice is stored in\n`localStorage` and is deliberately kept after logout, so the login page\nis then shown in the last language the user picked. A first-time visitor\nwith no stored preference gets French, the source locale. Adding the\nswitcher to the login page itself is tracked separately.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- Routing, the login page itself, and the forbidden/not-found pages are\nowned by other tickets (CPC-1977, CPC-1981, AUTH team). This PR only\nadds i18n markup on top of what already exists, per the team''s clarified\nscope. That is why the switcher sits in the header and not on the login\npage: adding a control to a page owned by another ticket would go beyond\nthat scope. Allowing a language choice before authentication is tracked\nseparately.\n- `@angular/localize` substitutes text the first time a template\nrenders, so switching language needs a page reload. This is a limitation\nof the official package, confirmed against\nhttps://angular.dev/api/localize/loadTranslations. The \"no reload\"\nwording of the original criterion was adjusted with the team.\n- The navbar labels and the sidenav items are still in English: they\nbelong to CPC-1971, which was merged on September 27, three days after\nthis ticket was written, and the sidenav entries are still placeholders\n(\"Dummy #1\", \"Dummy #2\"). They also live in TypeScript rather than a\ntemplate, so they need `$localize` tagged literals rather than `i18n`\nattributes. Translating them is tracked separately.\n- The catalogue is fetched with `fetch()` rather than `HttpClient` on\npurpose: `HttpClient` runs through `apiBaseUrlInterceptor` and\n`authInterceptor`, which would rewrite the URL and attach a bearer token\nto a static asset. The path is absolute because nginx serves `public/`\nat the site root in every environment.\n- `features/inventories/routes.spec.ts` needed `routes[0]?.component`.\nPR #1489 enabled `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` four days before that file\nwas added, so `routes[0].component` was a TS2532 error, and because\n`tsconfig.spec.json` compiles every spec as one program it stopped the\nwhole suite from compiling. Flagged for INVT to confirm.\n- One pre-existing failure remains in `app.spec.ts`: `app.html` contains\nonly `<router-outlet />` and has no `<h1>` for its assertion to find.\nNot touched by this PR.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de66655379a4a65d739042e5c89b3ba2f6e25f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/de66655379a4a65d739042e5c89b3ba2f6e25f67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/