e from compiling.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo, this PR does not call any API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, only frontend changes.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nBefore, no switcher and no footer, the interface only in English:\n\nAfter, FR and EN buttons in the header and a translated footer, French\nby default:\n\n**Login page, French (default):**\n\n<img width=\"1568\" height=\"675\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/154f43cb-374b-439a-89ea-d88165b9d91c\"\n/>\n\n**Login page, English:**\n\n<img width=\"1568\" height=\"675\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cd1eeab-68ba-4df8-abea-7deb32108b93\"\n/>\n\n**Home page, French (default):**\n\n<img width=\"1916\" height=\"821\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6ae1eba-805b-4555-aece-e4488ef1062e\"\n/>\n\n**Home page, English (after selecting EN in the header):**\n\n<img width=\"1876\" height=\"825\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1e467a5-6cb7-4af1-93ce-747e546f55e2\"\n/>\n\n> **Note on the English login screenshot:** the login page has no\nswitcher of its own, since the switcher lives in the header and the\nheader is inside the shell, behind the auth guard. English is reached by\nselecting EN from the header while signed in: the choice is stored in\n`localStorage` and is deliberately kept after logout, so the login page\nis then shown in the last language the user picked. A first-time visitor\nwith no stored preference gets French, the source locale. Adding the\nswitcher to the login page itself is tracked separately.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- Routing, the login page itself, and the forbidden/not-found pages are\nowned by other tickets (CPC-1977, CPC-1981, AUTH team). This PR only\nadds i18n markup on top of what already exists, per the team''s clarified\nscope. That is why the switcher sits in the header and not on the login\npage: adding a control to a page owned by another ticket would go beyond\nthat scope. Allowing a language choice before authentication is tracked\nseparately.\n- `@angular/localize` substitutes text the first time a template\nrenders, so switching language needs a page reload. This is a limitation\nof the official package, confirmed against\nhttps://angular.dev/api/localize/loadTranslations. The \"no reload\"\nwording of the original criterion was adjusted with the team.\n- The navbar labels and the sidenav items are still in English: they\nbelong to CPC-1971, which was merged on September 27, three days after\nthis ticket was written, and the sidenav entries are still placeholders\n(\"Dummy #1\", \"Dummy #2\"). They also live in TypeScript rather than a\ntemplate, so they need `$localize` tagged literals rather than `i18n`\nattributes. Translating them is tracked separately.\n- The catalogue is fetched with `fetch()` rather than `HttpClient` on\npurpose: `HttpClient` runs through `apiBaseUrlInterceptor` and\n`authInterceptor`, which would rewrite the URL and attach a bearer token\nto a static asset. The path is absolute because nginx serves `public/`\nat the site root in every environment.\n- `features/inventories/routes.spec.ts` needed `routes[0]?.component`.\nPR #1489 enabled `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` four days before that file\nwas added, so `routes[0].component` was a TS2532 error, and because\n`tsconfig.spec.json` compiles every spec as one program it stopped the\nwhole suite from compiling. Flagged for INVT to confirm.\n- One pre-existing failure remains in `app.spec.ts`: `app.html` contains\nonly `<router-outlet />` and has no `<h1>` for its assertion to find.\nNot touched by this PR.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvqGECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz5cQAFLrxEfUk9u4IDdM2x3ipmPJ\nR0o97Kl7WzCw3