:"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackyKBK","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/9483ba16c9dd2ae0b9c1cf67d261fece5fd4311b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:12:48Z","email":"167229877+JackyKBK@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JackyB"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:12:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VETS-CPC-1981): Update not-found and forbidden pages (#1540)\n\n**JIRA:** \n\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/69?selectedIssue=CPC-1981\n\n## Context:\nThis ticket makes it easier for employees (users) to recover from\nnot-found and forbidden errors. It implements a button that allows users\nto return to the home page after calling the error.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. Added a simple layout to the not-found and forbidden html files. \n2. Added a button with an event in the html pages.\n3. Added styling from the customer portal not-found and forbidden pages\nto ensure consistency.\n4. Added routing to the typescript files that takes the user to the\nhomepage.\n5. Deleted the basic rendering check in app.spec. This was causing\nerrors since the home page had changed and, if left, will cause further\nconflicts when the home page ticket is implemented.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nBefore: \n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-28 193929\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca04eb4c-e648-40ff-900b-6fcbf396b05d\"\n/>\nAfter:\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 133148\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54a89a92-b8c7-465b-84bc-4773e005c373\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48cb650a-646b-4066-b15c-810a5dea30d7\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nTo produce these screens, manually enter either of these at the end of\nthe page url:\n\n404 Not Found(/error/not-found)\nThe trigger is entering a non-existing url, example:\nhttps://petclinic-emp-portal.benmusicgeek.synology.me/apple will trigger\nthe not-found page. Prevents users from seeing hard crashes when\nentering old/deleted urls or invalid urls.\n\n403 Forbidden(/error/forbidden) \nThe trigger is an authenticated user trying to access an element outside\nof their permissions. Example: a vet tries to add or update a product.\n\nWhile the code does handle these errors, this feature is necessary to\ngive users a good UX and easily route them back to the home page instead\nof users receiving generic browser pages or the application crashing.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links","tree":{"sha":"804676be54b7edf9cff21b1d378e4bc3fdc09dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/804676be54b7edf9cff21b1d378e4bc3fdc09dfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/9483ba16c9dd2ae0b9c1cf67d261fece5fd4311b","verification":{"payload":"tree 804676be54b7edf9cff21b1d378e4bc3fdc09dfc\nparent 95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28\nauthor JackyB <167229877+JackyKBK@users.noreply.github.com> 1790824368 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790824368 -0400\n\nfeat(VETS-CPC-1981): Update not-found and forbidden pages (#1540)\n\n**JIRA:** \n\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/69?selectedIssue=CPC-1981\n\n## Context:\nThis ticket makes it easier for employees (users) to recover from\nnot-found and forbidden errors. It implements a button that allows users\nto return to the home page after calling the error.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. Added a simple layout to the not-found and forbidden html files. \n2. Added a button with an event in the html pages.\n3. Added styling from the customer portal not-found and forbidden pages\nto ensure consistency.\n4. Added routing to the typescript files that takes the user to the\nhomepage.\n5. Deleted the basic rendering check in app.spec. This was causing\nerrors since the home page had changed and, if left, will cause further\nconflicts when the home page ticket is implemented.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nBefore: \n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-28 193929\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca04eb4c-e648-40ff-900b-6fcbf396b05d\"\n/>\nAfter:\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 133148\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54a89a92-b8c7-465b-84bc-4773e005c373\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1020\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48cb650a-646b-4066-b15c-810a5dea30d7\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nTo produce these screens, manually enter either of these at the end of\nthe page url:\n\n404 Not Found(/error/not-found)\nThe trigger is entering a non-existing url, example:\nhttps://petclinic-emp-portal.benmusicgeek.synology.me/apple will trigger\nthe not-found page. Prevents users from seeing hard crashes when\nentering old/deleted urls or invalid urls.\n\n403 Forbidden(/error/forbidden) \nThe trigger is an authenticated user trying to access an element outside\nof their permissions. Example: a vet tries to add or update a product.\n\nWhile the code does handle these errors, this feature is necessary to\ngive users a good UX and easily route them back to the home page instead\nof users receiving generic browser pages or the application crashing.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvc+wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIJ8QAEdBTTlnvIKUy5FQLj2DcEQ4\nKUiOceFA5FEnxdyYhNtILqSgCssXv5HNHaX9NeEfOkQFoxzgYuwPw40Rg65NtWab\nUPn/w1E0QTBWOQDy62efzCeMunTfPwVmqDo3ZVGEUPRFdB7EuSPaB7StosrRPpeo\nuMN9bbbWWSyrKYNl9En2t9ph5LARMkO6ATMaMnsnmuxbtnJn0nY7AsEnqVODdIAj\nrLvYuPp/trdclSYukRgavXxICBEwSf6DH8H8AmZRPh3RsRtL14GMCd5ZqVtYWFcD\nJAzhVIypYFcjLjLmnaGuSUhbIAHknl7OAgi2GU7naIOK8ElhyJNlCgFh3cXE3nK7\nvIXdrHi6uBx4C7plcaw3tBqF+iNkgfP7AP3zDJlUgsJ8kZAixS6DNPUEhDzsFVcI\nbDZZow3hwqItpiYZvgk8RkvrhyIoy7ZOKZEjEAhWLOX7xplJ5gZSeTYOdaD26Fn9\n3hzZqofgH2Ah9c6VmEKXBEjseHYYnS8aGwcRjBSC2kCXScgzzf9LOKDKn4LIE5HE\nHKTGK7UopfFWpSSY/DMr+as1LtmI/7X3wi4yzhW42R8QEtSs8des7YygISzewMFU\nu/EG4kgsaYe13o2gPfXm4T00WatsEb2Ptb1KMQiaWSOXfBEVneGNnIPsBtzwKdGF\nhGALuY8mfcaqHnTQ5Nc5\n=Qwf3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T03:12:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/9483ba16c9dd2ae0b9c1cf67d261fece5fd4311b","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDk0ODNiYTE2YzlkZDJhZTBiOWMxY2Y2N2QyNjFmZWNlNWZkNDMxMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28","sha":"95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28"}],"sha":"9483ba16c9dd2ae0b9c1cf67d261fece5fd4311b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/9483ba16c9dd2ae0b9c1cf67d261fece5fd4311b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230245741?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vik-zl","id":230245741,"login":"vik-zl","node_id":"U_kgDODblFbQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vik-zl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T02:37:53Z","email":"zlateva.vik@gmail.com","name":"Viktoria Zlateva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T02:37:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(INVT-CPC-1996): create a supply page (#1503)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1996](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1996)\n\n## Context\n\nAdds a Supply page to the Employee Portal for a selected inventory.\nEmployees can view its supplies; admins and inventory managers can add,\nedit, and delete them.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not modify the `.vscode` folder.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added the `/invt/:inventoryId/supplies` route, Supply model, and\nstatus enum.\n- Added a Supply service that reads the existing inventory-products SSE\nendpoint through the project''s shared `SseClient` and uses the existing\nAPI for create, update, and delete requests.\n- Added a reusable shared table component. The Supply page provides its\ncolumns, status display, and role-restricted Edit and Delete actions.\n- Added a validated Add/Edit form. Cancelling clears edit state, and\nswitching to another supply clears the previous error and touched-field\nstate.\n- Made management controls update when the user''s roles change while the\npage is open.\n- Kept the table visible while the supply list refreshes after add,\nedit, or delete.\n- Labeled `productPrice` as “Cost Price” to clarify what the table\ndisplays.\n- Added an Angular Material deletion confirmation dialog and visible\nerrors when deletion fails or the inventory ID is missing.\n- Added tests for the Supply service, Supply page, and shared table.\n- Fixed an existing inventory route test''s indexed access so the Angular\ntest build can compile.\n\nThis change affects the Angular Employee Portal and uses existing\nbackend endpoints. It adds no new dependency.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\n\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\nBefore:\n<img width=\"1912\" height=\"1077\" alt=\"BeforeSupplyPage\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c2518bb-0b69-40a7-8697-7fcda68c159e\"\n/>\n\nAfter:\n<img width=\"1905\" height=\"980\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageNew\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a38aa8c-ad0e-49b3-b0f9-b40efca9d042\"\n/>\n\nAdd/Edit Supply form:\n\n<img width=\"1895\" height=\"972\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageAddForm\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d66f4d1-f243-4928-9bb3-6cddd6dafaff\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"975\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageEdit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1071e5-2cfa-49ae-b078-61c37a501c08\"\n/>\n\nDelete Dialog:\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"975\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageEdit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1071e5-2cfa-49ae-b078-61c37a501c08\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"957\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageDeleteDialog\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/671c7089-b638-46ac-8642-6d99c9034b85\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\n- The page reads `inventoryId` from the route and requests\n`/api/gateway/inventories/{inventoryId}/products`.\n- Add, Edit, and Delete controls use this feature''s role checks. Broader\nEmployee Portal access is addressed in #1497.\n- The backend currently rejects quantity 0, so supporting out-of-stock\nquantities needs a separate backend and frontend change.\n- The backend currently requires `productSalePrice`; its meaning for\nclinic inventory still needs a separate decision.\n- `npm run build` passed. The focused Supply page, Supply service, and\nshared table tests passed: 33 tests across 3 spec files.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\n- #1490 — dynamically changing inventory page\n- #1497 — employee guard for portal access\n\n---------","tree":{"sha":"6e6b2b3e4ae0d8cf426523b61fa226c60a4b874b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/6e6b2b3e4ae0d8cf426523b61fa226c60a4b874b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/95b97f5bd59f8e37206ab31ca1b927bd289e1a28","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e6b2b3e4ae0d8cf426523b61fa226c60a4b874b\nparent a6a8958edc4272cfd822e1c415c6767f87cc716e\nauthor Viktoria Zlateva <zlateva.vik@gmail.com> 1790822273 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790822273 -0400\n\nfeat(INVT-CPC-1996): create a supply page (#1503)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1996](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1996)\n\n## Context\n\nAdds a Supply page to the Employee Portal for a selected inventory.\nEmployees can view its supplies; admins and inventory managers can add,\nedit, and delete them.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not modify the `.vscode` folder.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added the `/invt/:inventoryId/supplies` route, Supply model, and\nstatus enum.\n- Added a Supply service that reads the existing inventory-products SSE\nendpoint through the project''s shared `SseClient` and uses the existing\nAPI for create, update, and delete requests.\n- Added a reusable shared table component. The Supply page provides its\ncolumns, status display, and role-restricted Edit and Delete actions.\n- Added a validated Add/Edit form. Cancelling clears edit state, and\nswitching to another supply clears the previous error and touched-field\nstate.\n- Made management controls update when the user''s roles change while the\npage is open.\n- Kept the table visible while the supply list refreshes after add,\nedit, or delete.\n- Labeled `productPrice` as “Cost Price” to clarify what the table\ndisplays.\n- Added an Angular Material deletion confirmation dialog and visible\nerrors when deletion fails or the inventory ID is missing.\n- Added tests for the Supply service, Supply page, and shared table.\n- Fixed an existing inventory route test''s indexed access so the Angular\ntest build can compile.\n\nThis change affects the Angular Employee Portal and uses existing\nbackend endpoints. It adds no new dependency.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?\n\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\nBefore:\n<img width=\"1912\" height=\"1077\" alt=\"BeforeSupplyPage\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c2518bb-0b69-40a7-8697-7fcda68c159e\"\n/>\n\nAfter:\n<img width=\"1905\" height=\"980\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageNew\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a38aa8c-ad0e-49b3-b0f9-b40efca9d042\"\n/>\n\nAdd/Edit Supply form:\n\n<img width=\"1895\" height=\"972\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageAddForm\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d66f4d1-f243-4928-9bb3-6cddd6dafaff\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"975\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageEdit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1071e5-2cfa-49ae-b078-61c37a501c08\"\n/>\n\nDelete Dialog:\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"975\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageEdit\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1071e5-2cfa-49ae-b078-61c37a501c08\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1882\" height=\"957\" alt=\"AfterSupplyPageDeleteDialog\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/671c7089-b638-46ac-8642-6d99c9034b85\"\n/>\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\n- The page reads `inventoryId` from the route and requests\n`/api/gateway/inventories/{inventoryId}/products`.\n- Add, Edit, and Delete controls use this feature''s role checks. Broader\nEmployee Portal access is addressed in #1497.\n- The backend currently rejects quantity 0, so supporting out-of-stock\nquantities needs a separate backend and frontend change.\n- The backend currently requires `productSalePrice`; its meaning for\nclinic inventory still needs a separate decision.\n- `npm run build` passed. The focused Supply page, Supply service, and\nshared table tests passed: 33 tests across 3 spec files.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\n- #1490 — dynamically changing inventory page\n- #1497 — employee guard for portal access\n\n---------","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvceBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdLMQAGJyYVw8lhCnFJ/Kv1H5kjxx\ne2QlgBuqo3n4R0CukA2zBb7WkrVGFTAE56aTmXNImwVGhx1MvJwgVBYIs5d9BFs2\nVdS7pvpqDB2Q4sDRm/ylNaGMVdCz3/gt0Jkkm+zYNil4TqEn9MpGRx5FqFbIbmPt\nSeL3hFbYRIy9lWRprkwrMiII/nrTt1HaOPQ04e9Rz4G75wj6idr6QnfrlmcsgZy9\nn1q1OGE7f3dmYMFbk7EmOkn1ZBlFe4PmHfC09tvGVdaEeMXMD68xQUgLjwiz+dN6\nypSd79c0FjMkmPYZONaQwzq3/67d+ZK19q6vn4rBNj3P8ntmSo1EhyHZtFtSFL5k\nZ9v1gvdlns0VlmNXNXengl4HgEYKbrtqHE+xI4adjlYeveDlO+Mdn4IfTh/YbrgS\nX91OdMnNEWVt0gPB81eMDEFMDo1AXA9xO6Ka6IVcDo/8Gq9w2OvmQJxJnHWe8S3J\ndlXLEU6s1UzAzVIFdAuquHq3xcBQ9GUaJGtM1EIMbve3ALU/bceM27d+rGogfDGv\n6789N6rR/uls+sRu8MskrSLYfWALyeJbj/UqXtO3elglCSJj7zlLuTQE8wyUGpXi\nn0nuj4rxncnVDPYSe9THyQewdgVgH8r+5nVDWPjkD8eDOgFg6mOwURsknQEU1zKQ\nSGpDV5+9AG98rw4ozBnt\n=XAY9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T02:37:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}"