down\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvb6/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfIwQADJcY4D53y3s6KCjHgJiczlS\n2X5wVY1uPRcwCxcQGxH2dp3VbpO04tngtPJdL/n3NB1cGNXyzT4bPNKj+aM0YSIi\nu23im/Bv5j1CfdBBZ1W04vnR86JhQT6DQcrk/0SkdrcbKj04AHmx4WDO2ZyV6QYU\nTjVMo21XyrIk60vuvEA1Y31uOl36iaghNspegoBKYaUj+oJcC4UDS03D+15a+2BO\nck/42jtkFmIn4I18wa9UGyBSFeMG6gQ9d9Iu41XJrihooQn9rpalT3q7+KmCN9Bc\nCpev4kYPSvh+H+Nbz0BGanJW2wO1irVlnup1GDj1I7UNdPbiRIkhgqlXsGo220sC\nbPmoilRiy1O/aKSRbVARUca3A2BSxXzI7v3Cb77XEIzrsl4NrnQjxbQIo3HYkHFC\n9udBedfcov6IcRyLHpb/McfWBHgFQHxgjCrn6gh0qfp7JDCIHKBoC+xMs7HEKBam\niIgI0+Ljn/rqtRXHjgrvl2lHw9sS0O1R6I/tFunN3utibtaCF/Tcj7yF7TChIMaS\nHNih0dqy1EdWgXmOdZhZnXVuM2mPkyeEIpXa3Iuk8rARA9fdUdWnhuEmyTfED0om\nb0r5uzg74oiWSMu+4qxmxKXBtcOj9MwK5bu/kWerGZwv6++f9IuWm6Dndy8W7ObR\nvZLv+zh7I38U4wqNgrQN\n=ebbr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T02:00:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/a6a8958edc4272cfd822e1c415c6767f87cc716e","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGE2YTg5NThlZGM0MjcyY2ZkODIyZTFjNDE1YzY3NjdmODdjYzcxNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/f78fc86f13c351cccd4c3faf144f307af427d66b","sha":"f78fc86f13c351cccd4c3faf144f307af427d66b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f78fc86f13c351cccd4c3faf144f307af427d66b"}],"sha":"a6a8958edc4272cfd822e1c415c6767f87cc716e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/a6a8958edc4272cfd822e1c415c6767f87cc716e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137190630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bats712","id":137190630,"login":"Bats712","node_id":"U_kgDOCC1c5g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f78fc86f13c351cccd4c3faf144f307af427d66b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:58:56Z","email":"137190630+Bats712@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Goncalves"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:58:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(PROD-CPC-1791): Display reviewer username and profile picture (#1539)\n\n**JIRA:** [[CPC-1791 — Display customer''s profile picture and username\nwhen posting a review]\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1791?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNjQxOTJkYzM4OTNkNDdlMzk1OTE5ZjFlNWUzYjNkOWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9\n\n## Context:\n\nProduct reviews previously displayed the rating and review text without\nidentifying the reviewer. This change displays the customer’s profile\npicture and a display name consisting of their first name and last\ninitial.\n\nFollowing review feedback, the display name replaces the login username\nto avoid publishing account login identifiers. Guests can view reviewer\ninformation without logging in, preserving the guest-shop access\nintroduced by CPC-1965.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo changes were made to `petclinic-frontend/.vscode`.\n\nBe sure to include **cgerard321** as a reviewer.\n\n**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the .vscode folder and add\na comment about it to their review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Products service:** Added the existing customer ID to rating\nresponses so the gateway can identify each reviewer.\n- **API gateway:** Added a service that retrieves the reviewer’s current\ncustomer profile and returns their first name, last initial, and profile\npicture.\n- Replaced `reviewerUsername` with `reviewerDisplayName` in the response\nmodel and frontend.\n- Removed the public username endpoint and its authentication exceptions\nintroduced in the earlier version of this PR.\n- **Customer Portal:** Displayed the reviewer’s name and picture on\nreview cards, with a default avatar for missing or failed images and a\ngeneric “Customer” label when the name is unavailable.\n- Changed edit/delete button visibility to check authentication and the\nauthor’s ID instead of comparing review text.\n- Corrected review-response parsing so embedded image data URLs do not\nbreak loading.\n- Adjusted review-card styling for smaller screens.\n- Updated tests to cover display names, profile updates, fallback\nbehavior, and guest access.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nNo. The frontend continues to use the v1 review endpoint.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo new service-to-service connections were introduced. The\nimplementation uses the existing gateway connections to the products and\ncustomer services.\n\nThe C4 L2 connections remain unchanged.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Before:** Review cards displayed the rating and review text without\nidentifying the reviewer.\n\n<img width=\"1225\" height=\"491\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd4546d4-1ece-49e7-a791-c884c556141b\"\n/>\n\n**After:** Review cards display the reviewer’s first name and last\ninitial, such as “Eduardo S.”, alongside their profile picture. A\ndefault avatar appears when no picture is available.\n\n<img width=\"1260\" height=\"575\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5c6cac1-8a1a-4883-a4c5-62101ba8435a\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\n- Profile information is retrieved when reviews are loaded, so profile\nchanges appear after reloading.\n- Guests can read reviews and reviewer information without a login\ncookie.\n- Login usernames are not included in the review response.\n- Personal-rating reads and review creation, editing, and deletion still\nrequire authentication.\n- No database migration is required.\n- The Jira acceptance criteria should be updated to reflect the agreed\nuse of a display name instead of a username.\n\n**Validation:**\n\n- Before the display-name revision, 40 targeted backend tests,\nTypeScript, focused lint, and Git whitespace checks passed.\n- These checks need to be rerun after the display-name revision.\n- Live Docker/browser validation remains pending. The previous local\npreview attempt was blocked by an SWC native compiler/cache-ownership\nissue.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\nCo-authored-by: Nathan Bessette <123912175+NateDev5@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"788ce54f3de4efca610a1aab45c0933a89e8048b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/788ce54f3de4efca610a1aab45c0933a89e8048b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/f78fc86f13c351cccd4c3faf144f307af427d66b","verification":{"payload":"tree 788ce54f3de4efca610a1aab45c0933a89e8048b\nparent 33c8a879f995559945adce5d436e1af17ec67b34\nauthor Eduardo Goncalves <137190630+Bats712@users.noreply.github.com> 1790816336 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790816336 -0400\n\nfeat(PROD-CPC-1791): Display reviewer username and profile picture (#1539)\n\n**JIRA:** [[CPC-1791 — Display customer''s profile picture and username\nwhen posting a review]\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1791?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNjQxOTJkYzM4OTNkNDdlMzk1OTE5ZjFlNWUzYjNkOWYiLCJwIjoiaiJ9\n\n## Context:\n\nProduct reviews previously displayed the rating and review text without\nidentifying the reviewer. This change displays the customer’s profile\npicture and a display name consisting of their first name and last\ninitial.\n\nFollowing review feedback, the display name replaces the login username\nto avoid publishing account login identifiers. Guests can view reviewer\ninformation without logging in, preserving the guest-shop access\nintroduced by CPC-1965.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\nNo changes were made to `petclinic-frontend/.vscode`.\n\nBe sure to include **cgerard321** as a reviewer.\n\n**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the .vscode folder and add\na comment about it to their review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Products service:** Added the existing customer ID to rating\nresponses so the gateway can identify each reviewer.\n- **API gateway:** Added a service that retrieves the reviewer’s current\ncustomer profile and returns their first name, last initial, and profile\npicture.\n- Replaced `reviewerUsername` with `reviewerDisplayName` in the response\nmodel and frontend.\n- Removed the public username endpoint and its authentication exceptions\nintroduced in the earlier version of this PR.\n- **Customer Portal:** Displayed the reviewer’s name and picture on\nreview cards, with a default avatar for missing or failed images and a\ngeneric “Customer” label when the name is unavailable.\n- Changed edit/delete button visibility to check authentication and the\nauthor’s ID instead of comparing review text.\n- Corrected review-response parsing so embedded image data URLs do not\nbreak loading.\n- Adjusted review-card styling for smaller screens.\n- Updated tests to cover display names, profile updates, fallback\nbehavior, and guest access.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\nNo. The frontend continues to use the v1 review endpoint.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo new service-to-service connections were introduced. The\nimplementation uses the existing gateway connections to the products and\ncustomer services.\n\nThe C4 L2 connections remain unchanged.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Before:** Review cards displayed the rating and review text without\nidentifying the reviewer.\n\n<img width=\"1225\" height=\"491\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd4546d4-1ece-49e7-a791-c884c556141b\"\n/>\n\n**After:** Review cards display the reviewer’s first name and last\ninitial, such as “Eduardo S.”, alongside their profile picture. A\ndefault avatar appears when no picture is available.\n\n<img width=\"1260\" height=\"575\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5c6cac1-8a1a-4883-a4c5-62101ba8435a\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\n- Profile information is retrieved when reviews are loaded, so profile\nchanges appear after reloading.\n- Guests can read reviews and reviewer information without a login\ncookie.\n- Login usernames are not included in the review response.\n- Personal-rating reads and review creation, editing, and deletion still\nrequire authentication.\n- No database migration is required.\n- The Jira acceptance criteria should be updated to reflect the agreed\nuse of a display name instead of a username.\n\n**Validation:**\n\n- Before the display-name revision, 40 targeted backend tests,\nTypeScript, focused lint, and Git whitespace checks passed.\n- These checks need to be rerun after the display-name revision.\n- Live Docker/browser validation remains pending. The previous local\npreview attempt was blocked by an SWC native compiler/cache-ownership\nissue.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\n\nCo-authored-by: Nathan Bessette <123912175+NateDev5@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvbBQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyQcQACKiMVdIBs9gClsobPlxlZqD\nGa+aRjJrSwPRCZCqqmMueO9E/6ARYZcGqOgNt42vKfcR/qtbAINkcmSY0cvsbOGG\nhH1r2xoNCrdLKmE2BzNptP/bEABvI2/HpoG8p27D4dAwBzz99r6+nq2v99wB+z6l\nTGsj4F4LUpN9E7jqW4CSZT8R88mfkYa4yIQirJA5Dv+r2YrxH+U41d02Xmq7eC2z\ncMmgn02mSu96Y+QKtGGHtVXCcZ7/T5sVeO5j9DBIM9xkrcezVJO+TIXNqEq5CKdo\na49qjD58tSFqqa0tRcP47jz50UyXrr8efdsBwaWCe0iv+SGKhoMN4i8b0bjlgTeJ\nwBPNsgdFow8IvV2AK5CdSwLn8vuLVfv5hJ9nH2wyNajUX1g2PQTT7g16gF8shiuq\nzs9+oIMYngcEQQhMKQKhiHAhPmoF57EtnG54F5u6/3rQBmBDm5fveXdZP9sbKRQ8\nvUAWcwbVnB3LStXwH2wI+Bl8m/yNWdgcSM8KV5MlLqPBSSGpadMTaWQnrpjr4MTe\n68GZC3H+0AF+aBU1HzpHYRF1nM0RT1HqgRVn/iizUMYxgaCNMPdIwvbcUF1qRtIR\nw6t83Y/KA5CFW1jR12gVp1w+HYWImNJ7vZNCLz7SZWVgHe+nursdS8aBTZc7YxGa\ndi7DTQdJGd5o5oh4BmcR\n=iSy8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T00:58:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/g