privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikegents","id":107361953,"login":"mikegents","node_id":"U_kgDOBmY2oQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikegents","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f6f5580be8e7bd43d8371cff3e88d9f43909d44e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:19:42Z","email":"107361953+mikegents@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mike Gents"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:19:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(PROD-CPC-1725): Change prod images to new file service (#1528)\n\n**JIRA:** [PROD-CPC-1725 — Change images to new file\nservice](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1725)\n\n## Context\n\nProduct images previously relied on the legacy image storage endpoints.\nThis PR adds Files Service support for new product image uploads,\nretrievals, replacements, and deletions while maintaining compatibility\nwith existing legacy images.\n\nExisting images are not migrated by this PR. Products Service now uses a\ndual-read strategy:\n\n1. Check the legacy `images` table.\n2. If no legacy image exists, request it from Files Service.\n3. If neither source returns an image, return the product with `image:\nnull`.\n\nAn unavailable image or Files Service outage therefore does not prevent\nthe catalog or product page from loading.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not change the `.vscode` folder.\n\n**Reviewers: please confirm this in your review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added Files Service support for creating products with images.\n- Stored the Files Service file ID on new and updated products.\n- Added optional embedded image data to product responses.\n- Added `includeImage` support to the v1:\n  - Product catalog endpoint.\n  - Product-details endpoint.\n  - Product-type endpoint.\n- Added v1 endpoints for replacing and deleting product images.\n- Added cleanup handling to prevent orphaned files when saving a product\nfails.\n- Added protection for shared and default images during replacement and\ndeletion.\n- Added dual-read compatibility:\n  - Existing images load from the legacy `images` table.\n  - New images load from Files Service.\n  - Missing or unavailable images return as `image: null`.\n- Added startup repair for missing built-in legacy image records still\nreferenced by seeded products.\n- Kept product-image behavior out of the v2 API.\n- Added `fileId` to the shared API Gateway and frontend file models.\n- Updated the customer frontend to request and render embedded product\nimages.\n- Updated product and bundle components to display Files Service image\ndata.\n- Updated cart, wishlist, recent-purchase, and recommendation views to\nretrieve the current image using `productId`.\n- Prevented stale image IDs stored in existing cart records from\ncontrolling the displayed image.\n- Retained legacy image-ID loading for components without a product ID.\n- Updated the employee product-creation flow to send image data with the\nproduct request.\n- Updated the employee product-edit flow to replace images through the\nnew image endpoint.\n- Updated employee product lists and details to display embedded images.\n- Added validation for required file name, file type, and file data\nfields.\n- Added typed API Gateway exceptions:\n  - `ProductNotFoundException` for HTTP 404.\n  - `ProductImageDependencyException` for HTTP 424.\n  - Existing typed exceptions remain in use for HTTP 400 and 422.\n- Removed the compatibility constructor that accepted an `imageId` but\nsilently discarded it.\n- Updated affected tests to use `ProductRequestDTO.builder()`.\n- Changed catalog image enrichment from sequential loading to ordered\nconcurrent loading:\n  ```java\n  flatMapSequential(productService::includeImage, 8)\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nValidation completed during development:\n\n- The complete Products Service `check` task passed.\n- Products Service JaCoCo verification passed its configured 90%\ninstruction-coverage requirement.\n- Final Products Service coverage was 90% instruction coverage and 75%\nbranch coverage.\n- Added 22 `FilesServiceClient` tests; all passed.\n- `FilesServiceClient` reached 99% instruction coverage and 75% branch\ncoverage.\n- Focused product-image tests passed, covering:\n  - Product creation with an image.\n  - Legacy image retrieval.\n  - Files Service image retrieval.\n  - Image replacement and deletion.\n  - Missing images.\n  - Files Service outages.\n  - Legacy lookup failures.\n  - Missing built-in image restoration.\n  - Protection against overwriting existing legacy images.\n- Focused API Gateway client and typed-exception tests passed.\n- Products Service controller tests passed after adding ordered\nconcurrent image loading.\n- Employee frontend targeted lint and TypeScript compilation passed.\n- Employee frontend production build passed.\n- Manual testing confirmed:\n  - Products can be created with images.\n  - Existing product images can be replaced.\n  - Product images can be deleted.\n  - Existing legacy images continue to load.\n  - Updated product images appear in cart-related views.\n  - Missing images do not prevent the catalog from loading.\n- Repository-wide CI passed after rerunning an intermittent Customers\nService integration test.\n- No database migration is required for this deployment.\n- No local database records are included in this PR.\n\nAI assistance: ChatGPT assisted with implementation planning,\ntroubleshooting, code changes, test creation, validation, and manual\ntest planning.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yanis Achamou <yanisachamou@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ed206d22a7376bb12793c1d3b7d2546307e2b4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/8ed206d22a7376bb12793c1d3b7d2546307e2b4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/f6f5580be8e7bd43d8371cff3e88d9f43909d44e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ed206d22a7376bb12793c1d3b7d2546307e2b4a\nparent 0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b\nauthor Mike Gents <107361953+mikegents@users.noreply.github.com> 1790792382 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790792382 -0400\n\nfeat(PROD-CPC-1725): Change prod images to new file service (#1528)\n\n**JIRA:** [PROD-CPC-1725 — Change images to new file\nservice](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1725)\n\n## Context\n\nProduct images previously relied on the legacy image storage endpoints.\nThis PR adds Files Service support for new product image uploads,\nretrievals, replacements, and deletions while maintaining compatibility\nwith existing legacy images.\n\nExisting images are not migrated by this PR. Products Service now uses a\ndual-read strategy:\n\n1. Check the legacy `images` table.\n2. If no legacy image exists, request it from Files Service.\n3. If neither source returns an image, return the product with `image:\nnull`.\n\nAn unavailable image or Files Service outage therefore does not prevent\nthe catalog or product page from loading.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not change the `.vscode` folder.\n\n**Reviewers: please confirm this in your review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added Files Service support for creating products with images.\n- Stored the Files Service file ID on new and updated products.\n- Added optional embedded image data to product responses.\n- Added `includeImage` support to the v1:\n  - Product catalog endpoint.\n  - Product-details endpoint.\n  - Product-type endpoint.\n- Added v1 endpoints for replacing and deleting product images.\n- Added cleanup handling to prevent orphaned files when saving a product\nfails.\n- Added protection for shared and default images during replacement and\ndeletion.\n- Added dual-read compatibility:\n  - Existing images load from the legacy `images` table.\n  - New images load from Files Service.\n  - Missing or unavailable images return as `image: null`.\n- Added startup repair for missing built-in legacy image records still\nreferenced by seeded products.\n- Kept product-image behavior out of the v2 API.\n- Added `fileId` to the shared API Gateway and frontend file models.\n- Updated the customer frontend to request and render embedded product\nimages.\n- Updated product and bundle components to display Files Service image\ndata.\n- Updated cart, wishlist, recent-purchase, and recommendation views to\nretrieve the current image using `productId`.\n- Prevented stale image IDs stored in existing cart records from\ncontrolling the displayed image.\n- Retained legacy image-ID loading for components without a product ID.\n- Updated the employee product-creation flow to send image data with the\nproduct request.\n- Updated the employee product-edit flow to replace images through the\nnew image endpoint.\n- Updated employee product lists and details to display embedded images.\n- Added validation for required file name, file type, and file data\nfields.\n- Added typed API Gateway exceptions:\n  - `ProductNotFoundException` for HTTP 404.\n  - `ProductImageDependencyException` for HTTP 424.\n  - Existing typed exceptions remain in use for HTTP 400 and 422.\n- Removed the compatibility constructor that accepted an `imageId` but\nsilently discarded it.\n- Updated affected tests to use `ProductRequestDTO.builder()`.\n- Changed catalog image enrichment from sequential loading to ordered\nconcurrent loading:\n  ```java\n  flatMapSequential(productService::includeImage, 8)\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nValidation completed during development:\n\n- The complete Products Service `check` task passed.\n- Products Service JaCoCo verification passed its configured 90%\ninstruction-coverage requirement.\n- Final Products Service coverage was 90% instruction coverage and 75%\nbranch coverage.\n- Added 22 `FilesServiceClient` tests; all passed.\n- `FilesServiceClient` reached 99% instruction coverage and 75% branch\ncoverage.\n- Focused product-image tests passed, covering:\n  - Product creation with an image.\n  - Legacy image retrieval.\n  - Files Service image retrieval.\n  - Image replacement and deletion.\n  - Missing images.\n  - Files Service outages.\n  - Legacy lookup failures.\n  - Missing built-in image restoration.\n  - Protection against overwriting existing legacy images.\n- Focused API Gateway client and typed-exception tests passed.\n- Products Service controller tests passed after adding ordered\nconcurrent image loading.\n- Employee frontend targeted lint and TypeScript compilation passed.\n- Employee frontend production build passed.\n- Manual testing confirmed:\n  - Products can be created with images.\n  - Existing product images can be replaced.\n  - Product images can be deleted.\n  - Existing legacy images continue to load.\n  - Updated product images appear in cart-related views.\n  - Missing images do not prevent the catalog from loading.\n- Repository-wide CI passed after rerunning an intermittent Customers\nService integration test.\n- No database migration is required for this deployment.\n- No local database records are included in this PR.\n\nAI assistance: ChatGPT assisted with implementation planning,\ntroubleshooting, code changes, test creation, validation, and manual\ntest planning.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yanis Achamou <yanisachamou@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVK+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASbkQAA9+wLkRfomd4DIulOEGIZFp\nh4jDHubOV1yaLGAGO7Wr6yiHCAr7Vl7RTtyHPOS32lpDt0lyBpaTEydgNABQ6z+9\n0Hx/ckuI6MAA4D91dWIy50W9ukXeDwD981DZTtFX+QJ3hIJDeOFYYHOyukys09cK\nHJ6oPfmbKU98b+NlE5p9NyD/yDd13Dyfk+o8bRIe4x53Sfnp13clraX2Kw+FfPVc\nM5NmkkI/IJdPZyyw2FmGF0j1HUvk8WIvkrZlUUhLkU97Ztq6wVIOqOU1AogGv5nO\nFJJBIEn8KjDdPyTSmxjq2yIu9cognBwdkj8he58vxgWuWMF3TRN9Pl4In13nTuww\nDRQhftCBkHZ8aG3eT+Evk2/0eO+t/FevJ1k/RCJu2I73fFW1X/NM+1SY5pKtpXE/\nvOa1x+pAThUVqBy/TdmBU6C0vLY8x6x/v2tOmGUxr49XENlKQh3jklJPyF35ul1M\nqso1isRSd1Ts6mT8XfmubRJIAaPSsDM/jiMBM7jHz3hQkCVieEKUzJmPvZ174OvH\nIjtA0kYeVWIdlQW9vP7CzgbFdpWYm4Eyd4a5QMtbb6OOXbDaa6NyBbQiLNaXDiKs\ndI7QuaJosWFdYWWwMZXhlU9T107gAk7sRYUmmmjlWN1/doMEkvfTKbdrB/2VeJYz\nPPHz8h04xy51LcpRAxCl\n=d+9R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:19:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/f6f5580be8e7bd43d8371cff3e88d9f43909d44e","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGY2ZjU1ODBiZThlN2JkNDNkODM3MWNmZjNlODhkOWY0MzkwOWQ0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b","sha":"0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b"}],"sha":"f6f5580be8e7bd43d8371cff3e88d9f43909d44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/f6f5580be8e7bd43d8371cff3e88d9f43909d44e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203453743?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ArushiNaik","id":203453743,"login":"ArushiNaik","node_id":"U_kgDODCB1Lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArushiNaik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:17:06Z","email":"arushi.a.naik@gmail.com","name":"Arushi Naik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:17:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(BILL-CPC-1877): Create a Reactive Unbounded Pagination Method (#1517)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[[(CPC-1877)](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1877&text=bill)](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1877&text=bill)\n\n## Context:\nThe billing API currently provides bounded pagination for filtered bill\nqueries. This ticket adds a reactive, unbounded streaming option so\nclients can retrieve all matching bills without the existing pagination\nlimit.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not make any changes to the `.vscode` folder in\n`petclinic-frontend`.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Added a reactive `getAllBillsStream()` method to the billing service\nusing `Flux<BillResponseDTO>`.\n- Added `GET /bills/stream` to the billing service with\n`text/event-stream` response type.\n- Preserved all existing bill filters.\n- Added the corresponding streaming client method in the API Gateway.\n- Added `/stream` endpoints to both V1 and V2 API Gateway bill\ncontrollers.\n- Configured the API Gateway to consume `text/event-stream` responses.\n- Added unit and integration tests for the billing service, billing\ncontroller, API Gateway V1/V2 controllers, and `BillServiceClient`.\n- Affected modules:\n  - `billing-service`\n  - `api-gateway`\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nYes. A corresponding `/stream` endpoint was added to the V2 API Gateway\ncontroller to provide the reactive streaming functionality through the\nV2 API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nYes. The API Gateway now communicates with the billing service through\nthe new `/bills/stream` endpoint.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNot applicable. This PR does not make any UI changes.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nKeep it short:\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- Added unbounded reactive streaming with `Flux<BillResponseDTO>`.\n- Reused existing bill filters.\n- Added API Gateway SSE support and integration tests.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone.","tree":{"sha":"3dbd3c9684f6e449b2af9e466f0846589cd03739","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/3dbd3c9684f6e449b2af9e466f0846589cd03739"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/0661c2398df0ad3b518ed6498bbb437b1191e52b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3dbd3c9684f6e449b2af9e466f0846589cd03739\nparent df9382e05e84e5742cf64bfcce0963818d635ed3\nauthor Arushi Naik <arushi.a.naik@gmail.com> 1790788626 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790788626 -0400\n\nfeat(BILL-CPC-1877): Create a Reactive Unbounded Pagination Method (#1517)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[[(CPC-1877)](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1877&text=bill)](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/804/backlog?selectedIssue=CPC-1877&text=bill)\n\n## Context:\nThe billing API currently provides bounded pagination for filtered bill\nqueries. This ticket adds a reactive, unbounded streaming option so\nclients can retrieve all matching bills without the existing pagination\nlimit.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not make any changes to the `.vscode` folder in\n`petclinic-frontend`.\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\n- Added a reactive `getAllBillsStream()` method to the billing service\nusing `Flux<BillResponseDTO>`.\n- Added `GET /bills/stream` to the billing service with\n`text/event-stream` response type.\n- Preserved all existing bill filters.\n- Added the corresponding streaming client method in