github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/533c60f28c94c678f1f51b27eedf84d75b7f3832","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDUzM2M2MGYyOGM5NGM2NzhmMWY1MWIyN2VlZGY4NGQ3NWI3ZjM4MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c","sha":"951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c"}],"sha":"533c60f28c94c678f1f51b27eedf84d75b7f3832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/533c60f28c94c678f1f51b27eedf84d75b7f3832"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204773783?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gvxng","id":204773783,"login":"Gvxng","node_id":"U_kgDODDSZlw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gvxng","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:01:43Z","email":"yanisachamou@gmail.com","name":"Yanis Achamou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T01:01:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(CART-CPC-1837): recommend products by product type (#1529)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/73?selectedIssue=CPC-1837\n## Context:\nWhat is the ticket about and why are we doing this change.\n\nCPC-1837 changes how recommendation purchases are created. Previously, a\nproduct was recommended only after it was purchased three or more times.\nRecommendations are now based on the productType of previously purchased\nproducts.\nAfter checkout, products with the same productType are added to the\ncustomer’s recommendations. Duplicate products are removed.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n\n- Replaced the purchase-count recommendation logic with\nproductType-based recommendations.\n- Added productType to ProductResponseModel.\n- Added a Product service call to retrieve products by type.\n- Removed duplicate recommendations using the product ID.\n- Converted matching products into CartProduct objects.\n- Saved the new recommendations during checkout.\n- Changes affect the Cart service and use an existing Product service\nendpoint.\n- Updated the checkout unit test to mock the Product service calls used\nby the new product-type recommendation logic.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why\n\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show reviewers what\nit looks like.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Agnesa <agnesaverenceanu@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d90a5ce6aa0a5fc4d2f52f8815ca57ee09563546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/d90a5ce6aa0a5fc4d2f52f8815ca57ee09563546"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c","verification":{"payload":"tree d90a5ce6aa0a5fc4d2f52f8815ca57ee09563546\nparent fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7\nauthor Yanis Achamou <yanisachamou@gmail.com> 1790730103 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790730103 -0400\n\nbug(CART-CPC-1837): recommend products by product type (#1529)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/73?selectedIssue=CPC-1837\n## Context:\nWhat is the ticket about and why are we doing this change.\n\nCPC-1837 changes how recommendation purchases are created. Previously, a\nproduct was recommended only after it was purchased three or more times.\nRecommendations are now based on the productType of previously purchased\nproducts.\nAfter checkout, products with the same productType are added to the\ncustomer’s recommendations. Duplicate products are removed.\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nIf the PR changes the .vscode folder, explain why in detail because it\nshould not.\nBe sure to include cgerard321 as a reviewer.\n\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\n\n- Replaced the purchase-count recommendation logic with\nproductType-based recommendations.\n- Added productType to ProductResponseModel.\n- Added a Product service call to retrieve products by type.\n- Removed duplicate recommendations using the product ID.\n- Converted matching products into CartProduct objects.\n- Saved the new recommendations during checkout.\n- Changes affect the Cart service and use an existing Product service\nendpoint.\n- Updated the checkout unit test to mock the Product service calls used\nby the new product-type recommendation logic.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nIf the PR uses the v2 API, explain why\n\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nIf the PR adds a new communication between services, make sure to update\nthe C4 L2.\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nIf this is a change to the UI, include before and after screenshots to\nshow the differences.\nIf this is a new UI feature, include screenshots to show reviewers what\nit looks like.\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nSpecific technical changes that should be noted\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nPull request links\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Agnesa <agnesaverenceanu@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvF93CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHWgQAFLyHqsMq85QpZ929PpzPktD\nHAaNboAcrQ11+kbuxwnCdc1vRmWEwh6cfxlQkbU9ATGduS7KrRUJ/0+VYaNeHEap\nfVygcdy3dmGoVKcOc2D1AAourqZO9FMGU8GRpLzHonVKEFfnETopS+m8B41ur3jF\nw3mJRQnh30zlvtuZoOOcE9Y6H78UkX37I3v8fY0mxLtb9qSNKxkHyzPxreah1k0d\nZ8OSW0NRH24TGj+XG+EpaKbA3a3GorfuQ4+OL8IEF+R46sdYGgnWglDNWGx4SEYm\n4Nr2pWeuJat6VOEyYis5Rmq2IIJqcCLZ/HLEmAdT2L+D+1y4u45Pc2e5ZaiQoE/n\npdIsVsYJ0g8mEkcTqliqB42hVA9XinKGAsCjPxEZt5Vq7k/MHjKGiWyHQbxIpd1P\nUM4L48xkjlnylPPRAYlUs1jmfXmrDUiEoPO7oNJxgaH2JJ4u8QBPtjcXuKOZpKdl\n7npcBN+B66iNejgo7dyb0R12GvgrF2ldkeMWVKFf0CpWRPNa+tSojVYOrusYWnDx\n+W5m18PmGf9STTiyr5y7E0ZtSM+Yxkq+ivIn7J5HWw00w5d2nTAmtLUtlPjIn6cY\nnceeRR3Vt2NjmSRSALflsKGzTjShCuJcddYt3jrHRB9dNYY/Sc8EbSP81wzv2ulC\nvGDltCE+8nppoLLLTXfi\n=R5rA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T01:01:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDk1MWM1NzA0OWUxMTZkMmRjYTg1MDdlYmIyNTczN2I2ODY1Yjg2MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7","sha":"fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7"}],"sha":"951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/951c57049e116d2dca8507ebb25737b6865b861c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63722895?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rami38","id":63722895,"login":"Rami38","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzIyODk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rami38","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:51:19Z","email":"63722895+Rami38@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Yacoub Bakayoko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:51:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-2003): Make Capitalization Behavior Consistent Across All Customer Filters (#1534)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2003\n\n## Context:\nThe Customers page filters (First Name, Last Name, Address, City,\nProvince,\nTelephone) used case-sensitive `.includes()` matching. A search for\n\"ontario\"\nwould return no results for a customer whose city is stored as\n\"Ontario\".\nThis ticket makes all 6 filters case-insensitive so users can search \nregardless of capitalization.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Updated the `filteredCustomers` logic in `AllCustomers.tsx` to\nlowercase\n  both the customer field value and the filter input before comparison, \n  making all 6 filters case-insensitive.\n- No other modules or services affected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n<img width=\"1850\" height=\"1092\" alt=\"cpc-2003-before-city-uppercase\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d31630f-0f52-496e-bcf1-a0d8ef770a5e\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1838\" height=\"1091\" alt=\"cpc-2003-after-city-uppercase\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/220fe821-5c00-48ef-9f28-eef995c02348\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nNo backend/Java code was modified, so Jacoco coverage is unaffected by\nthis\nchange. Verified manually against seeded customer data across all 6\nfilter\nfields.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nN/A\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yacoub Bakayoko <2431671@champlaincollege.qc.ca>","tree":{"sha":"56551c15e58c026aafd65c38af7593c177dcbe1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/56551c15e58c026aafd65c38af7593c177dcbe1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7","verification":{"payload":"tree 56551c15e58c026aafd65c38af7593c177dcbe1a\nparent c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58\nauthor Yacoub Bakayoko <63722895+Rami38@users.noreply.github.com> 1790725879 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790725879 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-2003): Make Capitalization Behavior Consistent Across All Customer Filters (#1534)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2003\n\n## Context:\nThe Customers page filters (First Name, Last Name, Address, City,\nProvince,\nTelephone) used case-sensitive `.includes()` matching. A search for\n\"ontario\"\nwould return no results for a customer whose city is stored as\n\"Ontario\".\nThis ticket makes all 6 filters case-insensitive so users can search \nregardless of capitalization.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- Updated the `filteredCustomers` logic in `AllCustomers.tsx` to\nlowercase\n  both the customer field value and the filter input before comparison, \n  making all 6 filters case-insensitive.\n- No other modules or services affected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n<img width=\"1850\" height=\"1092\" alt=\"cpc-2003-before-city-uppercase\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d31630f-0f52-496e-bcf1-a0d8ef770a5e\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1838\" height=\"1091\" alt=\"cpc-2003-after-city-uppercase\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/220fe821-5c00-48ef-9f28-eef995c02348\"\n/>\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nNo backend/Java code was modified, so Jacoco coverage is unaffected by\nthis\nchange. Verified manually against seeded customer data across all 6\nfilter\nfields.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nN/A\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Yacoub Bakayoko <2431671@champlaincollege.qc.ca>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvE73CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARXkQAIJ7uWEnh1c2V3TKbZTALWQK\nNWYInkgI3bLzXM9hybYySEdSgxYcVRZNO0c5jjgAPIgxCOlNubfMYvd4ygPa0f0B\n32QlOvraAhhOjXJJKvz0pQAIqGnW/EtrqAQ7FKLOogDSoRm4FXcTKZbU2ZHMNpmj\nb+e/XxTAgqluAQZ1g8Bx61pK/XPtnbFC0i5CDDY20+/1DkHFnyIanXg8yVjg3GSj\nOG+m4v5uVyyy7ilXXoidQpBZKtjyJImPuCbPYB4HqqOFMq1O0Fgbiy1K6mN9Z4Dl\nyDURYxb+5+ZO5B4YuQDHm3h0r/jSM6U30sTegJomHKlI464pJ/bi/sv3uIS7Xgy4\nVGFb6BBE+ZFymSiQAgxg/dcBMXTA+N/k4kT3oZyd+gVUMBLvccYFUPL+a/FepX8C\npHwdAeWAU/ULJ9bdDmv7UBMgILPHx5a5migAAn3JdWyC8PwSE6Cer/BCVp/75dt5\nJpwJWaKu4Sa9XsjmAcxKEygt+RTyQT0AdkQZod0qotULLgeB7HOXq3Gij30vuEIB\nYFL+7D/pSgNn0egKXQX7Flz+wX2lJ+4YabPw7mgmMrNEORm79mtL/lBwNwp2u0dz\n4Ki7p2Y7pVvpPwEJLI1a96l/c4oVZgQ5OSAzA6xlq9J3gFvUVPHVQe64e+gyVpJ8\nzleSkU2EWpW0zj7rma6P\n=Seof\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T23:51:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGZiZjA4OThmMjBiNzY0Njc4NDQ1YWFhOGNlMTFlOWNlZTM4MjBhYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58","sha":"c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58"}],"sha":"fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/fbf0898f20b764678445aaa8ce11e9cee3820ac7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/210409230?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamB-Git7","id":210409230,"login":"AdamB-Git7","node_id":"U_kgDODIqXDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamB-Git7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:07:26Z","email":"benikhlef.adam@gmail.com","name":"AdamB-Git7"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:07:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-2002): add confirmation and error messages for customer profile (#1533)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2002\n\n## Context:\nAs a customer, I want to see confirmation and error messages when I\ncreate or update my profile so I know if my changes worked or if\nsomething needs to be fixed. Before this change, the Edit Profile page\ngave no feedback: a successful update just went back to Home, and a\nfailed update was only logged in the console. Province was also a free\ntext field, so customers could save misspelled or invalid provinces.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- **Edit Profile** (`UpdateCustomerForm.tsx`):\n  - Shows a success toast (\"Profile updated successfully\") after saving\n- Shows an error toast if saving fails, instead of only logging to the\nconsole\n- Telephone must be exactly 10 digits (same rule as the backend), with a\nclear message under the field\n  - Province is now a dropdown instead of free text\n- **Sign Up** (`SignUp.tsx`): Province is now a dropdown instead of free\ntext. Sign Up already had a confirmation screen and shows backend errors\n(like \"email already exists\"), so nothing else changed there.\n- Added `validateTelephone()` to\n`features/customers/utils/validation.ts`\n- Added a shared list of Canadian provinces and territories in\n`features/customers/utils/provinces.ts`\n- Updated the Sign Up Playwright test to select the province from the\ndropdown instead of typing it\n- Only affects the customer frontend. No backend changes, and the\nadmin/receptionist customer forms were not changed.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. It uses the existing v1 customer endpoints (`useV2: false`).\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n**Edit Profile: before**\nProvince and telephone accepted anything, and only empty fields were\nchecked.\n<img width=\"1110\" height=\"867\" alt=\"Before1\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9ba6680-728f-40b0-bdaa-a027f8d5d397\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"846\" alt=\"Before2\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/188f9e74-0b5d-4f13-b3a5-cd999777cb3e\"\n/>\n\n**Edit Profile: after**\nProvince is a dropdown, the telephone must be exactly 10 digits, and a\nconfirmation shows after saving.\n<img width=\"1310\" height=\"876\" alt=\"AfterValidation\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85ae2121-ff84-43a6-b135-6eaededa12fa\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1265\" height=\"495\" alt=\"Success message\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5de9551-5e10-4641-b9a7-2ef8f7d949c7\"\n/>\n\nThe same province dropdown was also added to the Sign Up page.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- The success toast is shown before `navigate()`. It still shows on the\nHome page because `ToastProvider` wraps the whole app in `main.tsx`.\n- The error toast uses our own message instead of the backend message,\nbecause the gateway returns a technical message for customer update\nerrors (e.g. \"422 Unprocessable Entity from PUT\nhttp://customers-service-reactive:8080/...\").\n- The province list was copied from `AdminUpdateCustomerForm.tsx` into a\nshared file used by the customer forms. The admin form was not changed\nand still has its own copy.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone","tree":{"sha":"aef4f409d9232f3bb045d43a5ecf43bc2f5ca1fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/aef4f409d9232f3bb045d43a5ecf43bc2f5ca1fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58","verification":{"payload":"tree aef4f409d9232f3bb045d43a5ecf43bc2f5ca1fe\nparent be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66\nauthor AdamB-Git7 <benikhlef.adam@gmail.com> 1790723246 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790723246 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-2002): add confirmation and error messages for customer profile (#1533)\n\n**JIRA:** https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-2002\n\n## Context:\nAs a customer, I want to see confirmation and error messages when I\ncreate or update my profile so I know if my changes worked or if\nsomething needs to be fixed. Before this change, the Edit Profile page\ngave no feedback: a successful update just went back to Home, and a\nfailed update was only logged in the console. Province was also a free\ntext field, so customers could save misspelled or invalid provinces.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n- **Edit Profile** (`UpdateCustomerForm.tsx`):\n  - Shows a success toast (\"Profile updated successfully\") after saving\n- Shows an error toast if saving fails, instead of only logging to the\nconsole\n- Telephone must be exactly 10 digits (same rule as the backend), with a\nclear message under the field\n  - Province is now a dropdown instead of free text\n- **Sign Up** (`SignUp.tsx`): Province is now a dropdown instead of free\ntext. Sign Up already had a confirmation screen and shows backend errors\n(like \"email already exists\"), so nothing else changed there.\n- Added `validateTelephone()` to\n`features/customers/utils/validation.ts`\n- Added a shared list of Canadian provinces and territories in\n`features/customers/utils/provinces.ts`\n- Updated the Sign Up Playwright test to select the province from the\ndropdown instead of typing it\n- Only affects the customer frontend. No backend changes, and the\nadmin/receptionist customer forms were not changed.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo. It uses the existing v1 customer endpoints (`useV2: false`).\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n**Edit Profile: before**\nProvince and telephone accepted anything, and only empty fields were\nchecked.\n<img width=\"1110\" height=\"867\" alt=\"Before1\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9ba6680-728f-40b0-bdaa-a027f8d5d397\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"846\" alt=\"Before2\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/188f9e74-0b5d-4f13-b3a5-cd999777cb3e\"\n/>\n\n**Edit Profile: after**\nProvince is a dropdown, the telephone must be exactly 10 digits, and a\nconfirmation shows after saving.\n<img width=\"1310\" height=\"876\" alt=\"AfterValidation\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85ae2121-ff84-43a6-b135-6eaededa12fa\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1265\" height=\"495\" alt=\"Success message\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5de9551-5e10-4641-b9a7-2ef8f7d949c7\"\n/>\n\nThe same province dropdown was also added to the Sign Up page.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n- The success toast is shown before `navigate()`. It still shows on the\nHome page because `ToastProvider` wraps the whole app in `main.tsx`.\n- The error toast uses our own message instead of the backend message,\nbecause the gateway returns a technical message for customer update\nerrors (e.g. \"422 Unprocessable Entity from PUT\nhttp://customers-service-reactive:8080/...\").\n- The province list was copied from `AdminUpdateCustomerForm.tsx` into a\nshared file used by the customer forms. The admin form was not changed\nand still has its own copy.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvESuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH4gQAJSzxy4XWFvz87FEZaH+1z0n\nGqdHk00cTtmGvSZQmRj73FqmgbreP3njrWvaN9qmKZio+ZFHJwqRURERto+84bPP\n9j2x/IF1TBUP8yJCmLtyU6gm765BhtK/xdaGXlx27xi6fgJA7YMOCiz/AS2ze7Fj\ns0xtLnb63qD3ncdncMwiu4etq64/c7FmeVpLA7DP7b/bDRb4lqNqRqLIIigLN/LG\n17UcmmHcUgiB+n8ecBaBJ68orF9gupmqK3B0XTdf6fpmIst5NRii2ZSX7Ts/OZfT\nTohn/RWw1fc/SrhyTXJnjIR38dCyL3w8UqOX9D5NViisgp78z3P492vhMgKvdrLF\nJLKcDyvGT9R+KBKbdAkNHZbao6R9IfkkvhHB4IzO956zsQiK3e80VvWn+HYO1m/a\nVQkl/UHrdqzbRK2jcE98CGHsc9CGOCKVISw+TMwwR/Qe+4HoWBuUuwgyyCp2xcrS\nfUA9lY1FAlmhIiTIWxOvzhEbTRL7n0wC3xwk22ZMTS2Y11Vfpbjskh6XlOlqEp64\nY+KAqby1oBJFYIyHX9FI4ZRgm+H/kZLAitM10EhYjPvJwimXxpdv5kGQP43lX/Sz\nMz+t+PiH7zKqZvaeoNEONYi5BsywO4xBTrrYpqeWwu0g5p3fZqZckoCTk/vWoIDv\nwZmDOLZJEji86MVx4HHP\n=Wcs1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T23:07:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGMyNmVkYTU1OWI0Y2I4YTk4MDdhYmFhYjQ0ODM4NWE2NWMwNThjNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66","sha":"be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66"}],"sha":"c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/c26eda559b4cb8a9807abaab448385a65c058c58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230245567?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MellonCat","id":230245567,"login":"MellonCat","node_id":"U_kgDODblEvw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MellonCat","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:49:30Z","email":"kyle.galbraith07@gmail.com","name":"Kyle Galbraith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:49:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bug(BILL-CPC-1986): Fix Duplicate GETbills Endpoint Mapping (#1496)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1986)\n\n## Context:\nTo fix the duplicate `/bills` endpoint mapping between `getAllBills` and\n`getAllBillsByPage`. Both methods were mapped to the same `/bills` path,\ncausing ambiguity between retrieving all bills and retrieving paginated\nbills. The endpoints are being separated to use distinct paths for each\noperation.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\napi-gateway:\n\n- Added a dedicated V2 /bills endpoint mapping for getAllBills\n- Changed the V2 paginated bills endpoint from /bills to\n/bills/paginated\n- Removed /bills from the V1 paginated bills endpoint mapping to\neliminate the duplicate mapping\n- Separated MockServer configurations for GET /bills and GET\n/bills/paginated\n- Updated MockServer response content types for the corresponding\nendpoints\n- Updated V2 BillController integration tests for the new endpoint\nmappings\n\nbilling-service:\n\n- Changed the paginated bills endpoint from /bills to /bills/paginated\n- Updated pagination integration tests to use /bills/paginated\n- Updated pagination unit tests to use /bills/paginated\n\npetclinic-frontend:\n\n- Updated the paginated bills API request to use the V1 Gateway\npagination endpoint.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, It only modifies an existing communication between the API Gateway\nand Billing Service\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kyle Galbraith <kyleg@WHYWORLD>\nCo-authored-by: Arushi Naik <arushi.a.naik@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"87b8d394db708c4d2f2b16b851f883ef6dd842d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/87b8d394db708c4d2f2b16b851f883ef6dd842d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66","verification":{"payload":"tree 87b8d394db708c4d2f2b16b851f883ef6dd842d5\nparent 0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167\nauthor Kyle Galbraith <kyle.galbraith07@gmail.com> 1790700570 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790700570 -0400\n\nbug(BILL-CPC-1986): Fix Duplicate GETbills Endpoint Mapping (#1496)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1986)\n\n## Context:\nTo fix the duplicate `/bills` endpoint mapping between `getAllBills` and\n`getAllBillsByPage`. Both methods were mapped to the same `/bills` path,\ncausing ambiguity between retrieving all bills and retrieving paginated\nbills. The endpoints are being separated to use distinct paths for each\noperation.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nWhat are the various changes and what other modules do those changes\naffect.\nThis can be bullet point or sentence format.\napi-gateway:\n\n- Added a dedicated V2 /bills endpoint mapping for getAllBills\n- Changed the V2 paginated bills endpoint from /bills to\n/bills/paginated\n- Removed /bills from the V1 paginated bills endpoint mapping to\neliminate the duplicate mapping\n- Separated MockServer configurations for GET /bills and GET\n/bills/paginated\n- Updated MockServer response content types for the corresponding\nendpoints\n- Updated V2 BillController integration tests for the new endpoint\nmappings\n\nbilling-service:\n\n- Changed the paginated bills endpoint from /bills to /bills/paginated\n- Updated pagination integration tests to use /bills/paginated\n- Updated pagination unit tests to use /bills/paginated\n\npetclinic-frontend:\n\n- Updated the paginated bills API request to use the V1 Gateway\npagination endpoint.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, It only modifies an existing communication between the API Gateway\nand Billing Service\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kyle Galbraith <kyleg@WHYWORLD>\nCo-authored-by: Arushi Naik <arushi.a.naik@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+waCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3lIQAHH4uxtQc2aU/GxySBIXYvac\nn6ig7LmhAZ8r1a9+QV0pGozfvLZG90LlGlh8I2nv4l1oDAM3gRPHEgE7toYiU3gT\n4OGiBfdth+lb/nBMUnkGk1cPl2k4KeSpDaWVk83HnuupxLo+gCJ2prVXI2ceHTpu\npPcaI/Gt2FIPDfzqZNEy8DYRHWbGqbO5s3fWYouUT5sedYVnO/vEFHlDwkcflAtv\nN8P0fnNZUdGJsaB0ueZiRJfLQySiTwDwL9EC7Umq7ntYKM7YvYk10lBnQtcKNFQw\n8RRYnx8PQT2Ho9RczLQwExa4guNRyOxwkCpLRiucRX/qdno6V4vyphmTdRbFps1k\n/sna/pa55e7yhTHbyot9NaeAMbGDccCG/Sg5c0yitEGjV5ugRvtA07atiT4lKHZ4\nyENwtqODhyZxdzWxtx5v00tAR6zC5Z9KFngg3+RqMcnizUTYwe/ER56O1ttCtI6D\ngUwHrfPoIAInzS4qv9Svw/0G7tW9iNCnyDh5VCUVbtqQv/uttcJILA1oLYZKSDsO\nugKgA4tQy5KCm06OIpN+XpV/oRBszdaoEypxlQLc9Cw3jgFdw21UnYYZlss0jVTl\no6bY5dOjEtebUmSyX+71iXQL6QzTi4enG+B3xtomKpvOHqF3hoX9NSb3ezyJYcJD\nmSXOPELXBxDPncjl1e+E\n=5orq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:49:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGJlMTg1YjYyZjJlNTFiZjZiNjJiY2Q1YTBjZGEyY2Q0MDZjMThlNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167","sha":"0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167"}],"sha":"be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/be185b62f2e51bf6b62bcd5a0cda2cd406c18e66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180322279?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ilianadeleke","id":180322279,"login":"ilianadeleke","node_id":"U_kgDOCr9_5w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilianadeleke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:29:17Z","email":"iladelek@gmail.com","name":"IlianLawson_DEV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:29:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-1962): i18n setup internationalization and add LanguageSwitcher (#1484)\n\n- Configure i18n setup in src/utils/i18n.ts\n- Add EN/FR translation JSON files\n- Create reusable LanguageSwitcher component in shared/components\n- Clean up App.tsx router configuration\n- Add i18n setup documentation for the team\n\n### **Context:**\nAs a Customer, I need to be able to change the language of the page from\nEnglish to French. Implementing internationalization (French) (i18n) on\nthe customer portal to meet the following criteria:\n\n- System must be able to support English and French\n\n- The application must have English as a default language\n\n- The language must be able to be changed manually\n\n- All UI text must be changed according to the set language\n\n\n### **Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:**\nNo, this PR does not change the .vscode folder. cgerard321 has been\nadded as a reviewer.\n\n### **Changes:**\n- Configured i18n setup in src/utils/i18n.ts and imported it in main.tsx\n- Added translation JSON files for English and French in src/locales/\n- Created reusable LanguageSwitcher.tsx component in\nsrc/shared/components/language/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\n- Added i18n_README.md to document how to add translations to components\n\n### **Does this use the v2 API?:**\nNo\n### \n### **Does this add a new communication between services?:**\nNo\n\n### **Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs):**\n\nBefore: All text was hardcoded in English with no option to switch\nlanguages.\n<img width=\"1866\" height=\"936\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3199df4b-7ffc-46d6-975d-32aa19f3560b\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1643\" height=\"538\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f636cc21-793d-4144-a8bd-f22a5a0c17fc\"\n/>\n\n\nAfter: Language toggle button added to switch between English and\nFrench.\n\n<img width=\"1540\" height=\"425\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/734328b0-587f-4200-96c8-21c1199407f3\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"20e8235a8fabffbff4ceec912e0ad6414b308e14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/20e8235a8fabffbff4ceec912e0ad6414b308e14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/0e5a56855e937277b798385f376a2a5ed4f7f167","verification":{"payload":"tree 20e8235a8fabffbff4ceec912e0ad6414b308e14\nparent 647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7\nauthor IlianLawson_DEV <iladelek@gmail.com> 1790699357 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790699357 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-1962): i18n setup internationalization and add LanguageSwitcher (#1484)\n\n- Configure i18n setup in src/utils/i18n.ts\n- Add EN/FR translation JSON files\n- Create reusable LanguageSwitcher component in shared/components\n- Clean up App.tsx router configuration\n- Add i18n setup documentation for the team\n\n### **Context:**\nAs a Customer, I need to be able to change the language of the page from\nEnglish to French. Implementing internationalization (French) (i18n) on\nthe customer portal to meet the following criteria:\n\n- System must be able to support English and French\n\n- The application must have English as a default language\n\n- The language must be able to be changed manually\n\n- All UI text must be changed according to the set language\n\n\n### **Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:**\nNo, this PR does not change the .vscode folder. cgerard321 has been\nadded as a reviewer.\n\n### **Changes:**\n- Configured i18n setup in src/utils/i18n.ts and imported it in main.tsx\n- Added translation JSON files for English and French in src/locales/\n- Created reusable LanguageSwitcher.tsx component in\nsrc/shared/components/language/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\n- Added i18n_README.md to document how to add translations to components\n\n### **Does this use the v2 API?:**\nNo\n### \n### **Does this add a new communication between services?:**\nNo\n\n### **Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs):**\n\nBefore: All text was hardcoded in English with no option to switch\nlanguages.\n<img width=\"1866\" height=\"936\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3199df4b-7ffc-46d6-975d-32aa19f3560b\"\n/>\n\n<img width=\"1643\" height=\"538\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f636cc21-793d-4144-a8bd-f22a5a0c17fc\"\n/>\n\n\nAfter: Language toggle button added to switch between English and\nFrench.\n\n<img width=\"1540\" height=\"425\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/734328b0-587f-4200-96c8-21c1199407f3\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+ddCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM8UQACHOPnZ3ChQyZBapZNZM2ADS\nuhmN/GqPXBZLvzNouc/ap9mL0gq9QWrm1cKsyX+KYT6sh5pUROUTuvmGvlp0QqL4\npljRaGjL2uU3wowPBDv3JLKxy4NL8e3fYy5kOMbdg4zwClm8tDG0xFYt4HcrfvVb\n26PyxtVCY6DPrnGEmWdAvtE5OYrzDgBKHKibk+tZzml7iN602EN7bZuMWpQVIrZx\nqOmT8d9C3bOjuEtbcXWfI5rCFW6SfhnS4XRepzeAzte40gY+9E7i3M+quw+JDM+L\nG3aj2l7n0DVD8QbNEs22W23qgTrje3xeESYqN3ql1uct1chjN8oY7dlNWlEee7iu\nBaN3oXB/ghmzLDe3fRbiv436wgptXwvNG0Rx2rPuq3Lhv65iGKnxm6a2G+VHVzfo\nrm8+QV5n+1kIdqBG94b0xJAnEUHBv+yZBAJkPUuNjTv9xgIE1D+LMysVZcjpSNiY\nMM49Di1wNRtZGQYeh6bh7BvFbF8L/gWdooZeXRec2wYfy/r+OdTyZiq3NM0RSHSr\n6N0TLewb+6h5V9du6k+e8TGD7jFNmS/aTIFMMW3y7ySwSC60poGWCkZ/D0UCKL2T\nwB2HnnFjmijAOTiYUkN+F3U9cQT+NsNSNejwx1E4c3H+qa5szrlUIlZMSTB7Hj1I\nxy+QUXVCQU6Lmata6+hG\n=8uTE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:29:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/e