github.com/users/JannoLawendy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JannoLawendy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JannoLawendy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JannoLawendy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JannoLawendy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JannoLawendy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T03:24:37Z","email":"jannohany24@yahoo.com","name":"JannoLawendy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T03:24:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(BILL-CPC-1987): Prevent an already-paid bill from being paid again (#1519)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1987](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1987)\n## Context:\nThe processPayment() method allowed a bill with the PAID status to be\npaid again. This change prevents duplicate payments by returning an\nerror when a bill is already paid.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n## Changes\n- Added validation in BillServiceImpl.processPayment() to check whether\nthe bill status is already PAID.\n- Returns InvalidPaymentException with the message “Bill has already\nbeen paid.”\n- Prevents an already-paid bill from being saved again.\n- Prevents another payment-confirmation email from being sent.\n- Keeps the bill status as PAID.\n- Confirmed that UNPAID and OVERDUE bills can still be paid.\n- Added a unit test confirming that an already-paid bill is rejected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNot applicable. This PR only changes backend payment validation and unit\ntests.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe following tests passed using Java 17:\n\n- processPayment_Success()\n- processPayment_OverdueBill_ShouldBecomePaid()\n- processPayment_AlreadyPaidBill_ShouldReturnError()\n- Full Billing Service test suite\n\nBuild result: BUILD SUCCESSFUL\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Arushi Naik <arushi.a.naik@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"63f5f061d6b50e9eb0ceca025966b00b00764661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/63f5f061d6b50e9eb0ceca025966b00b00764661"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7","verification":{"payload":"tree 63f5f061d6b50e9eb0ceca025966b00b00764661\nparent e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691\nauthor JannoLawendy <jannohany24@yahoo.com> 1790652277 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790652277 -0400\n\nfix(BILL-CPC-1987): Prevent an already-paid bill from being paid again (#1519)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1987](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1987)\n## Context:\nThe processPayment() method allowed a bill with the PAID status to be\npaid again. This change prevents duplicate payments by returning an\nerror when a bill is already paid.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n## Changes\n- Added validation in BillServiceImpl.processPayment() to check whether\nthe bill status is already PAID.\n- Returns InvalidPaymentException with the message “Bill has already\nbeen paid.”\n- Prevents an already-paid bill from being saved again.\n- Prevents another payment-confirmation email from being sent.\n- Keeps the bill status as PAID.\n- Confirmed that UNPAID and OVERDUE bills can still be paid.\n- Added a unit test confirming that an already-paid bill is rejected.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNot applicable. This PR only changes backend payment validation and unit\ntests.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\nThe following tests passed using Java 17:\n\n- processPayment_Success()\n- processPayment_OverdueBill_ShouldBecomePaid()\n- processPayment_AlreadyPaidBill_ShouldReturnError()\n- Full Billing Service test suite\n\nBuild result: BUILD SUCCESSFUL\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)\nNone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Arushi Naik <arushi.a.naik@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquy91CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMV0QAA8N8g+9chk/CLdvEWJB//Rq\nhufnHO4Pry/xpd5v5OzlbYKAnefP8FKBmUt1qqKcE+FzcMXvIS99xIMWoU91+G8t\nU6ZNLI+96w4M/xLhQ59iCSmoblnmIQmBCQU3dZPAaCjR8vmxI0SDjyJw4UISB9A0\nsmIrZdGQ7DforwcohuM9FOGc7JEEXpk5h5tlccHN3hGWUjMJ0D6T+a3PmdrraBjO\npoJn4xAu8L3Foy76jNTo7lc2p4FSK9nOXhuqs4hveDjChUV9toMJ72v1Bh6iufbg\nv0YZ3LpygNyBbMqJMkeLF9tfuSWgK/7dOPq/UZe5fJ0D6G9802C/kqIJmjPnAtqI\nM4mo45O6wB/RiJz20dqgzoJyWkOKWpMkYUX0RRXcBdLOVEgzdP5cEXT2oGytp0GW\nBDOlXPDTh36sA07L12tLY162HcVp+o9Db8UBDtsffiH1JPLwtYSUvfuoksF8bwaA\nQ3ZqmeS7APF0yLN1w6akEtsFZwZfv43CLip93Do8kCuErZEuymDJRF2yBNlR1Xct\nr+GhE7KPMFeBm17UzEn3DVPtSNVhu/F6W7x64VxI8UjssXWUoZaGXtjr+DHw/JdF\nomNJ0o/NP6bRSrAWI/JahFBA4Lo26M6czkgpXrtBkO+Kl+MTPWVUd+2CZFWpPVQo\nP5J4/JzimIIT4Gduxngg\n=oX3q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T03:24:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDY0N2U2ZGFjMjBhZjg0ZTNjYWQ2N2IyODZjNGVmZDE2YzE4MzlhYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691","sha":"e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691"}],"sha":"647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/647e6dac20af84e3cad67b286c4efd16c1839ac7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137190630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bats712","id":137190630,"login":"Bats712","node_id":"U_kgDOCC1c5g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bats712","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:29:49Z","email":"137190630+Bats712@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Goncalves"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:29:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(PROD-CPC-1965): Allow guests to browse the shop (#1511)\n\n**JIRA:** [CPC-1965 — Allow guests to browse the\nshop](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1965)\n\n## Context:\nGuests previously had to log in to access the shop. This change allows\nthem to browse products, product details, images, bundles, and published\nreviews without an account.\n\nCart, wishlist, and review actions still require login. The changes are\nin the Customer Portal (petclinic-frontend) and API gateway.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not change the .vscode folder.\n\n**Reviewers: please confirm this in your review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n- Moved the Shop navigation link outside the logged-in-only section.\n- Removed ProtectedRoute from the products and product-details routes.\n- Added authentication checks before cart, wishlist, and review actions\nso guests are redirected to login.\n- Updated product details to fetch personal ratings only when\nauthenticated and clear that state for guests.\n- Updated guest bundle loading to use a read-only product request\ninstead of the helper that first sends an authenticated tracking PATCH.\n- Hid the bundle Add to Cart button from guests.\n- Allowed anonymous reads of the catalog, bundles, product images, and\npublished reviews through the v1 gateway endpoints.\n- Added GuestShopAccessTest.java with 18 cases covering public reads and\nrejected guest requests to protected endpoints.\n\nAffected modules: petclinic-frontend and api-gateway. No old frontend\nfiles were changed (doubleChecked=True).\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo new v2 API usage was introduced. The shop reads involved in this\nchange use the existing v1 endpoints under /api/gateway. No v2 endpoint\npermissions were changed.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This change uses existing gateway-to-service connections, so no C4\nL2 update is needed.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n**Before:** The Shop navigation link was hidden from guests, and product\npages required login.\n\n**After:** Guests can open the shop and view products without logging\nin. Selecting an account action, such as Add to Cart, redirects them to\nlogin.\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nValidation during development:\n- 58 gateway tests passed, including the 18 new guest-access cases.\n- TypeScript and focused frontend lint checks passed.\n- A live guest browser check loaded 8 products, their images, and 3\nbundles.\n\n\nAI assistance: ChatGPT assisted with planning, troubleshooting, and\nvalidation. Details are recorded in the Dev Log.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)","tree":{"sha":"972732aafc46b64ca0722655940c5c7ac5311bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/972732aafc46b64ca0722655940c5c7ac5311bc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691","verification":{"payload":"tree 972732aafc46b64ca0722655940c5c7ac5311bc8\nparent 41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d\nauthor Eduardo Goncalves <137190630+Bats712@users.noreply.github.com> 1790648989 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790648989 -0400\n\nfeat(PROD-CPC-1965): Allow guests to browse the shop (#1511)\n\n**JIRA:** [CPC-1965 — Allow guests to browse the\nshop](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1965)\n\n## Context:\nGuests previously had to log in to access the shop. This change allows\nthem to browse products, product details, images, bundles, and published\nreviews without an account.\n\nCart, wishlist, and review actions still require login. The changes are\nin the Customer Portal (petclinic-frontend) and API gateway.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo. This PR does not change the .vscode folder.\n\n**Reviewers: please confirm this in your review comments.**\n\n## Changes\n- Moved the Shop navigation link outside the logged-in-only section.\n- Removed ProtectedRoute from the products and product-details routes.\n- Added authentication checks before cart, wishlist, and review actions\nso guests are redirected to login.\n- Updated product details to fetch personal ratings only when\nauthenticated and clear that state for guests.\n- Updated guest bundle loading to use a read-only product request\ninstead of the helper that first sends an authenticated tracking PATCH.\n- Hid the bundle Add to Cart button from guests.\n- Allowed anonymous reads of the catalog, bundles, product images, and\npublished reviews through the v1 gateway endpoints.\n- Added GuestShopAccessTest.java with 18 cases covering public reads and\nrejected guest requests to protected endpoints.\n\nAffected modules: petclinic-frontend and api-gateway. No old frontend\nfiles were changed (doubleChecked=True).\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo new v2 API usage was introduced. The shop reads involved in this\nchange use the existing v1 endpoints under /api/gateway. No v2 endpoint\npermissions were changed.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo. This change uses existing gateway-to-service connections, so no C4\nL2 update is needed.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n**Before:** The Shop navigation link was hidden from guests, and product\npages required login.\n\n**After:** Guests can open the shop and view products without logging\nin. Selecting an account action, such as Add to Cart, redirects them to\nlogin.\n\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nValidation during development:\n- 58 gateway tests passed, including the 18 new guest-access cases.\n- TypeScript and focused frontend lint checks passed.\n- A live guest browser check loaded 8 products, their images, and 3\nbundles.\n\n\nAI assistance: ChatGPT assisted with planning, troubleshooting, and\nvalidation. Details are recorded in the Dev Log.\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquyKdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4KwQADW5DZ5q0ZoK4YEr+/rV8ZUb\nobLeqRD1hPnHJJfk7AkEO6AN4c5FmYfcvliuf7IqRBa5zBzcSTOzKV1g9ORysrG6\n/tDq6BUMR+qqFW7x4h4yes+bjQ4+tg5K0bdLmkJnB0T/HOIkRM5sJDR38Wz0fuRt\nmXjMM5dDCG3WEbiRYIgPrAWBNCcMFVqwXLdv0tQbAJcNVVdXOGHmXJIbSPh3ZrDF\nK1QH0I9AInm3VkUWob1X1GzA0hz6hzMsakjatykTJ3FpJe3428rfnmClH8g8fsOb\nV3Fj9jylHLqpIJTFAGUekX4+KTpw56ba9IOSYajDWCnhl8ysYUrRufgO2yiRe+pL\ngT2oDyx3knJzBHyorVub+Xa2Mqxrk17oXHK6i2cDyzRTBgU9vRL6W4vMDXJsAG6W\nqRhbFdcwragKOI5d4bhjc7EHWUAoN6otwxxR3rJ9FoUkFWyB4PYnWetwL40gEdNG\nmtA5r13/aXeIcn713UjyAumBVEAV2m27CZ2GZDN3CQc10kB2s+uYmm89nXE40pIJ\nMfLQYEzCBThLs8HzYLj0A8PBaj/UnM8PF14VYOKxp7VCQWneNmZfEgtKaetw1Vuz\nMdvEcuGHbbsq+L/9tr6m72ZYnBwjxEDIYm72q0OzFt/qoM0vHlyalFlSlTMmJp7j\nrwncgGlf4V0hg7y9c2vV\n=WJo6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T02:29:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKGU0OTNiZmE5YzgyMzY2ZTk4NTlmYjQ2YmI2YzA0ZWUwNzY3Mzk2OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d","sha":"41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d"}],"sha":"e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/e493bfa9c82366e9859fb46bb6c04ee076739691"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167229698?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AarushP06","id":167229698,"login":"AarushP06","node_id":"U_kgDOCfe5Ag","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AarushP06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:47:53Z","email":"167229698+AarushP06@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AarushP06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:47:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(PROD-CPC-1785): convert Product Add, Details, and Update pages to modals (#1513)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1785](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1785)\n\n  ## Context\n\nThe goal of CPC-1785 is to change the Angular Product Add, Details, and\nUpdate pages into modal dialogs in the new employee frontend.\n\nThis improves the employee portal experience by allowing users to manage\nproducts without navigating away from the Product List page.\n\n\n  ## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not modify the `.vscode` folder in\n`petclinic-frontend`.\n\n  ## Changes\n\n  - Implemented the Product List page in `employee-frontend`.\n  - Added the Add Product Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added the Product Details Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added the Product Update Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added Product models, interfaces, and enums.\n  - Added ProductService API methods.\n  - Added ImageService for image upload and retrieval.\n  - Added product image thumbnails to the Product List.\n  - Added image upload during product creation.\n  - Added optional image replacement during product updates.\n- Added validation for required fields, price, quantity, and image\ntypes.\n  - Added loading and error states.\n- Added Product List refresh after successful Add and Update operations.\n- Added unit tests for the Product page, dialogs, ProductService, and\nImageService.\n  - Updated the CPC-1785 development log.\n\n  ## Does this use the v2 API?\n\n  No. This PR uses the existing v1 API endpoints.\n\n  ## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo. This PR does not add communication between services. It only uses\nthe existing Product and Image API endpoints through the API Gateway.\n\n  ## Before and After UI\n\n  This is a new Product feature in the employee frontend.\n\n  ### Before\n\nBefore Product UI<img width=\"1679\" height=\"882\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d3c2d33c-536d-45af-8d77-9e21f8c47651\"\n/>\n\n  ### After\n\nProduct List: <img width=\"1679\" height=\"914\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d662b598-a2c0-4846-aec8-5bd20fe54eaf\"\n/>\n\nAdd Product Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"958\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc9567d8-e882-478b-8066-22b4c2dea0bb\"\n/>\n\nProduct Details Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"883\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f410154-e23a-4195-9713-c411e44dc4d5\"\n/>\n\nProduct Update Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"913\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47764579-ab71-4eb1-807c-d9b6de1286d4\"\n/>\n  ## Dev notes\n\n  - Implementation is limited to `employee-frontend`.\n  - The legacy AngularJS frontend was not modified.\n  - `petclinic-frontend` was not modified.\n  - No backend Java, database, Gradle, or `.vscode` files were modified.\n  - Add and Update are restricted to `ADMIN` and `INVENTORY_MANAGER`.\n  - Details is read-only.\n- The existing image is preserved when no replacement image is selected.\n  - Product tests passed: 12/12.\n  - Angular build passed.\n- The full test suite has one unrelated existing failure in\n`app.spec.ts` because it expects an outdated “Hello…” heading.\n- Angular reports an existing duplicate `@layout/*` warning in\n`tsconfig.json`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dylan Brassard <71225455+DylanBrass@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"194cbdb7f15248c7db0dbfd07ef2fac842caec8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/194cbdb7f15248c7db0dbfd07ef2fac842caec8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/41197b055f3d6b9b80c64fc9859d19b52c14647d","verification":{"payload":"tree 194cbdb7f15248c7db0dbfd07ef2fac842caec8f\nparent 3a4923250d7fd4d6f51cafca45a1a55f9ecfeffe\nauthor AarushP06 <167229698+AarushP06@users.noreply.github.com> 1790642873 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790642873 -0400\n\nfeat(PROD-CPC-1785): convert Product Add, Details, and Update pages to modals (#1513)\n\n**JIRA:**\n[CPC-1785](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1785)\n\n  ## Context\n\nThe goal of CPC-1785 is to change the Angular Product Add, Details, and\nUpdate pages into modal dialogs in the new employee frontend.\n\nThis improves the employee portal experience by allowing users to manage\nproducts without navigating away from the Product List page.\n\n\n  ## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?\n\nNo. This PR does not modify the `.vscode` folder in\n`petclinic-frontend`.\n\n  ## Changes\n\n  - Implemented the Product List page in `employee-frontend`.\n  - Added the Add Product Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added the Product Details Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added the Product Update Angular Material dialog.\n  - Added Product models, interfaces, and enums.\n  - Added ProductService API methods.\n  - Added ImageService for image upload and retrieval.\n  - Added product image thumbnails to the Product List.\n  - Added image upload during product creation.\n  - Added optional image replacement during product updates.\n- Added validation for required fields, price, quantity, and image\ntypes.\n  - Added loading and error states.\n- Added Product List refresh after successful Add and Update operations.\n- Added unit tests for the Product page, dialogs, ProductService, and\nImageService.\n  - Updated the CPC-1785 development log.\n\n  ## Does this use the v2 API?\n\n  No. This PR uses the existing v1 API endpoints.\n\n  ## Does this add a new communication between services?\n\nNo. This PR does not add communication between services. It only uses\nthe existing Product and Image API endpoints through the API Gateway.\n\n  ## Before and After UI\n\n  This is a new Product feature in the employee frontend.\n\n  ### Before\n\nBefore Product UI<img width=\"1679\" height=\"882\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d3c2d33c-536d-45af-8d77-9e21f8c47651\"\n/>\n\n  ### After\n\nProduct List: <img width=\"1679\" height=\"914\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d662b598-a2c0-4846-aec8-5bd20fe54eaf\"\n/>\n\nAdd Product Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"958\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc9567d8-e882-478b-8066-22b4c2dea0bb\"\n/>\n\nProduct Details Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"883\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f410154-e23a-4195-9713-c411e44dc4d5\"\n/>\n\nProduct Update Dialog<img width=\"1679\" height=\"913\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47764579-ab71-4eb1-807c-d9b6de1286d4\"\n/>\n  ## Dev notes\n\n  - Implementation is limited to `employee-frontend`.\n  - The legacy AngularJS frontend was not modified.\n  - `petclinic-frontend` was not modified.\n  - No backend Java, database, Gradle, or `.vscode` files were modified.\n  - Add and Update are restricted to `ADMIN` and `INVENTORY_MANAGER`.\n  - Details is read-only.\n- The existing image is preserved when no replacement image is selected.\n  - Product tests passed: 12/12.\n  - Angular build passed.\n- The full test suite has one unrelated existing failure in\n`app.spec.ts` because it expects an outdated “Hello…” heading.\n- Angular reports an existing duplicate `@layout/*` warning in\n`tsconfig.json`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dylan Brassard <71225455+DylanBrass@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquwq5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALE4QAInhZEc0lB9ptHMqB1du8hBV\nMRnqNxu7ts60qx9bOh8QMEuiJ1N+W8zbuAKwih8iG0o4dwyHdPz+LL60DDH3fSVK\nmYeJ0E6R9eu9DFf2WMhljGGpcJgzWIJZKDOjEwa0aXV4Yd94eiLk6AJYm7semlYf\nJ4CvBWSb+RfXjojU22BFI6r7kSizPxE7IXMn+4gloSCKMGJgRQvCF8J37gMx29QK\nDg4aZaAM1smHHgcfibcX1Vz6yFq6Vi49JfK/qaDEwX6cg9ZhjsOhBrW