ercontent.com/u/208994289?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rainarra","id":208994289,"login":"rainarra","node_id":"U_kgDODHT_8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rainarra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/6ab9f31a6b729e1a9a96b817aeff44518cbf4a93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:17:06Z","email":"awintle@hotmail.com","name":"Alexandra wintle"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:17:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-1953): Standardize customer terminology in pet management (#1506)\n\n**JIRA:** CPC-1953\n\n## Context:\nin this ticket i standardized the ubiquitous language from owner to\ncustomer.\n\nThe goal of this ticket was to change the pet management parts of the\nproject from Owner to Customer. I updated pet IDs, routes, method names,\nmodels, frontend pages, and tests. I also updated the API Gateway and\ncustomer service so the new Customer pet routes work, while keeping old\nOwner methods where needed so other parts of the project do not crash.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n Changed pet-related `ownerId` fields to `customerId`.\n\n Updated pet DTOs and models in the customer service and API Gateway.\n\nUpdated the pet service, routes, API Gateway, frontend pages, models,\nand related files to use Customer terminology instead of Owner,\nincluding renaming addPetForOwner.ts and UpdateOwnerPetPage.tsx.\n\nUpdated pet-related unit and integration tests so that everything would\npass and be able to merge.\n\nKept legacy Owner compatibility methods where required so existing Owner\nand Visit functionality didnt cause any conflict so that we can merge.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThis PR updates customer pet management terminology and routes in the\nfrontend.\n\nBefore:\n- Pet management still used Owner terminology in some places.\n\nAfter:\n- Customer pet management uses Customer terminology consistently this\nway there is no confusion between customer and owner.","tree":{"sha":"217d8ec0f2f142db8b554ea25012bcba100e9503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/217d8ec0f2f142db8b554ea25012bcba100e9503"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/6ab9f31a6b729e1a9a96b817aeff44518cbf4a93","verification":{"payload":"tree 217d8ec0f2f142db8b554ea25012bcba100e9503\nparent c824e160170bb642c3c65e963ca627265ff4da25\nauthor Alexandra wintle <awintle@hotmail.com> 1790615826 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790615826 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-1953): Standardize customer terminology in pet management (#1506)\n\n**JIRA:** CPC-1953\n\n## Context:\nin this ticket i standardized the ubiquitous language from owner to\ncustomer.\n\nThe goal of this ticket was to change the pet management parts of the\nproject from Owner to Customer. I updated pet IDs, routes, method names,\nmodels, frontend pages, and tests. I also updated the API Gateway and\ncustomer service so the new Customer pet routes work, while keeping old\nOwner methods where needed so other parts of the project do not crash.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo.\n\n## Changes\n Changed pet-related `ownerId` fields to `customerId`.\n\n Updated pet DTOs and models in the customer service and API Gateway.\n\nUpdated the pet service, routes, API Gateway, frontend pages, models,\nand related files to use Customer terminology instead of Owner,\nincluding renaming addPetForOwner.ts and UpdateOwnerPetPage.tsx.\n\nUpdated pet-related unit and integration tests so that everything would\npass and be able to merge.\n\nKept legacy Owner compatibility methods where required so existing Owner\nand Visit functionality didnt cause any conflict so that we can merge.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\nNo\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nThis PR updates customer pet management terminology and routes in the\nfrontend.\n\nBefore:\n- Pet management still used Owner terminology in some places.\n\nAfter:\n- Customer pet management uses Customer terminology consistently this\nway there is no confusion between customer and owner.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquqESCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnscQAGUMxqqZCEZIluqXcAu+Nb1a\n7eM53BTWufxXMXvTw1hS8D9LwfW/0cWe4cuaPkmOkPkm9YmwBmY1LYBjRAmHF0TK\nHys0e5g6AFCK9+PpXEK/o6tXd+Q7n4edcWv9Xt5TgB15TEOWHrVJUrSJDD83oVMq\nS5X+kb4DZVRKPSD5jVYQGg2py/2pdiL31aKYPM5eBm+PQt8Ldw8PJaAL9ZJHWPrM\nCAtFRuzP9ruBPXwawLfea4Vr04a6Cd9fxUL15JY4OP5wQF03145p75skb0l8emge\nbWfo9deUNh0vVRdmJBqEiIf+m7CthI3nIRHaC48ghcbUhMJDp/zsRD7mQf+xoiqX\nqrbMxkFbjk0jPD0GXRuwx0K5C7YDT9njG76K6MWrGiT4SdNMeWXs3S30hCFUURJ6\n6gGhwFQy5daMzXZla12aKJOfkrlFkDSEOHEAn1nE1hqVxhd1IKdisI1FWyb9x3SU\nfoJ2jbN9DxoLHYMcaUJkWy99PMSFLzEBM9FyR9aSFpB7d3Vtid+4VS12HHbdRbJ2\nQwq3FdRClvQym9UzlA/4LTNeRe7aWaaFzfXVfx7tI886aWEhyDN1qGz4MnifIdzb\nGWl84X3cv96TsKh8jIZ4FPJZWpY13Sb8hTK02fV3UKBjZa1PJEQIK2+NC81DfpJw\nDPXDGsRCMA6p5B+OSl0l\n=S53E\n-----END PGP SIGNATU