ub.com/users/Chewquy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Chewquy","id":188070621,"login":"Chewquy","node_id":"U_kgDOCzW63Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chewquy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/04c00fdcdcfa0d0a0fc53e5d9ad61d8c0a5bc4d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:00:13Z","email":"thomas.angers@icloud.com","name":"Thomas Angers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:00:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(CUST-CPC-1950): Standardize customer terminology in customer service and customer front end (#1498)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/14?selectedIssue=CPC-1950\n## Context:\nAs an employee, I want the customer list and customer details to use\ncustomer instead of owner so the wording is clear and consistent, this\nwill relieve confusion (conformity to Ubiquitus language)\n\nThis ticket includes the customer list, customer details page, and the\nfrontend and backend changes needed to make them use the same Customer\nterminology.\n\nAs a user, I want all customer management features to use Customer\nterminology instead of Owner terminology so the system uses clear and\nconsistent wording.\n\nThis includes customer list, details, add, update, profile management,\nphotos, frontend, backend, API Gateway, files, exceptions, and tests\nrelated directly to the customer.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nI changed every use of the Owner terminology by Customer in every Owner\nfile in the backend and in the front end.\nThis affects the other services because some endpoints were changed, so\nif a service is calling on our endpoint, they will have to change it.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, but it affects the communication\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNo change to the UI, but the text has changed for owners to customers in\nevery place where owners was used.","tree":{"sha":"bee1a8c167b645c71227b8802de085361e49c6d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/bee1a8c167b645c71227b8802de085361e49c6d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/04c00fdcdcfa0d0a0fc53e5d9ad61d8c0a5bc4d4","verification":{"payload":"tree bee1a8c167b645c71227b8802de085361e49c6d1\nparent ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea\nauthor Thomas Angers <thomas.angers@icloud.com> 1790604013 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790604013 -0400\n\nfeat(CUST-CPC-1950): Standardize customer terminology in customer service and customer front end (#1498)\n\n**JIRA:**\nhttps://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CPC/boards/14?selectedIssue=CPC-1950\n## Context:\nAs an employee, I want the customer list and customer details to use\ncustomer instead of owner so the wording is clear and consistent, this\nwill relieve confusion (conformity to Ubiquitus language)\n\nThis ticket includes the customer list, customer details page, and the\nfrontend and backend changes needed to make them use the same Customer\nterminology.\n\nAs a user, I want all customer management features to use Customer\nterminology instead of Owner terminology so the system uses clear and\nconsistent wording.\n\nThis includes customer list, details, add, update, profile management,\nphotos, frontend, backend, API Gateway, files, exceptions, and tests\nrelated directly to the customer.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\nNo\n\n\n<span style=\"color:red\">**Reviewers need to check for any changes to the\n.vscode folder and add a comment about it to their review\ncomments.**</span>\n\n## Changes\nI changed every use of the Owner terminology by Customer in every Owner\nfile in the backend and in the front end.\nThis affects the other services because some endpoints were changed, so\nif a service is calling on our endpoint, they will have to change it.\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\nNo\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\nNo, but it affects the communication\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\nNo change to the UI, but the text has changed for owners to customers in\nevery place where owners was used.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqunLtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8MsQAI81nIoAOPeCkfAB7O2gjVsU\nCxdqUKGQsmwsSWSeOqeKZ4pLJRoKeUbaUtTD2EoBcJ1u1z70KL6LHaSadvgfVvVC\nID7kEsBG1WPCBwCGxHxOMVUqfgnTKoyFRgt5PzsGA2luGvKrz1zkRs87W5oLmgvZ\nAByr4IAPm1Qw1K0brVGjqtXjqRz/wVU4rfItA0rlE2C2+1KUYHZ1wM54U8PLco5W\n7GtwYLHL4ln7lvM5c3GOfgWWCrCDIlPZJwlzGZQefcWk2sCOem6VB+GyCUwz4Fnh\nFpHEnYRvsJbpJDq9cRbTYh6sZLe6vUUIrBNU75teMPgSGbcDUJTZaoRksarsZ5Kd\nwY4m+2rxkBpWW//MiJxPjRXgTVSqIWnYs6CQlpWJwFMvksYUUZxSZnfhbRC2CFh3\nnK+lP4HwSaCMALQltDgdt7FPCAvOc9hgRifEzmEV/kpYFpTEtn3nugcbaeHtniuv\ndJcf9LGwQOWfWWYkgCO1BRflFLrdHtoh7lZ5K8Xi/uPSv8QnYZekSYZkWwiZgzut\n0vDSOWtb6SmlscU0Kssy/oRT31e2IvDQAaamt9dXWx6TO//T8Nu6xczX3q1xRA1h\nVyiE9D3TTRT9IknJI7cft3yalCLgbTDjMR6Ra8HxvlKLI8r9Qhj0Awa2z8FoSBGD\nkggujIvxKY7o2WWmSWi/\n=lE53\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T14:00:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/04c00fdcdcfa0d0a0fc53e5d9ad61d8c0a5bc4d4","node_id":"C_kwDOF4d909oAKDA0YzAwZmRjZGNmYTBkMGEwZmM1M2U1ZDlhZDYxZDhjMGE1YmM0ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commit/ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea","sha":"ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea"}],"sha":"04c00fdcdcfa0d0a0fc53e5d9ad61d8c0a5bc4d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/04c00fdcdcfa0d0a0fc53e5d9ad61d8c0a5bc4d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181739404?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DanMoraru","id":181739404,"login":"DanMoraru","node_id":"U_kgDOCtUfjA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanMoraru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/commits/ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:50:13Z","email":"2431625@champlaincollege.qc.ca","name":"DanMoraru"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:50:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(AUTH-CPC-1973): use employee guard for portal access (#1497)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1973?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWI1MjliMjEzYzI0NDYyMzhlMDhmODFjMGY1NWFhOTQiLCJwIjoiaiJ9)\n\n## Context:\n\nThis PR addresses **AUTH-CPC-1973: Add role-based access to Employee\nPortal (Angular FE)**.\n\nThe Employee Portal already has authentication and an existing\n`employeeGuard`, but the employee route was not using that guard\ncorrectly for all supported employee roles. The goal of this change is\nto make sure authenticated employees with the supported employee roles\ncan access the Employee Portal while preserving the existing Customer\nPortal authentication behavior.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThere are no changes to the `.vscode` folder in `petclinic-frontend`.\nThe PR is limited to the Employee Portal route authorization.\n\n\n## Changes\n\n* Updated the Employee Portal route in `app.routes.ts` to use the\nexisting `employeeGuard`.\n* The route now uses:\n  `authGuard(), customerRedirectGuard, employeeGuard`\n* Reuses the existing role checks instead of adding duplicate role logic\nto the route.\n* The existing `employeeGuard` already handles the supported employee\nroles:\n\n  * `ADMIN`\n  * `VET`\n  * `RECEPTIONIST`\n  * `INVENTORY_MANAGER`\n* Removed unrelated frontend changes that were initially added while\ninvestigating the ticket, keeping the final PR scoped to the\nauthorization requirement.\n* No changes were made to the Customer Portal authentication flow.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThis change only affects Angular frontend route authorization and does\nnot use the v2 API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThere is no new communication between services. This PR only changes\nfrontend route guard behavior.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Not applicable.**\n\nThis PR does not introduce or modify the visual UI. The change affects\nroute access/authorization only.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nThe final functional change is limited to the Employee Portal route in\n`app.routes.ts`.\n\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)","tree":{"sha":"8c68f13a1d7684bd968b41430236830417a2db84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/trees/8c68f13a1d7684bd968b41430236830417a2db84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cgerard321/champlain_petclinic/git/commits/ecd9955210a8c5f31a023323424533e239fd77ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c68f13a1d7684bd968b41430236830417a2db84\nparent 81279161040fa6e8e071d796f9609b74b40eeaa3\nauthor DanMoraru <2431625@champlaincollege.qc.ca> 1790603413 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790603413 -0400\n\nfeat(AUTH-CPC-1973): use employee guard for portal access (#1497)\n\n**JIRA:** [link to jira\nticket](https://champlainsaintlambert.atlassian.net/browse/CPC-1973?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiOWI1MjliMjEzYzI0NDYyMzhlMDhmODFjMGY1NWFhOTQiLCJwIjoiaiJ9)\n\n## Context:\n\nThis PR addresses **AUTH-CPC-1973: Add role-based access to Employee\nPortal (Angular FE)**.\n\nThe Employee Portal already has authentication and an existing\n`employeeGuard`, but the employee route was not using that guard\ncorrectly for all supported employee roles. The goal of this change is\nto make sure authenticated employees with the supported employee roles\ncan access the Employee Portal while preserving the existing Customer\nPortal authentication behavior.\n\n## Does this PR change the .vscode folder in petclinic-frontend?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThere are no changes to the `.vscode` folder in `petclinic-frontend`.\nThe PR is limited to the Employee Portal route authorization.\n\n\n## Changes\n\n* Updated the Employee Portal route in `app.routes.ts` to use the\nexisting `employeeGuard`.\n* The route now uses:\n  `authGuard(), customerRedirectGuard, employeeGuard`\n* Reuses the existing role checks instead of adding duplicate role logic\nto the route.\n* The existing `employeeGuard` already handles the supported employee\nroles:\n\n  * `ADMIN`\n  * `VET`\n  * `RECEPTIONIST`\n  * `INVENTORY_MANAGER`\n* Removed unrelated frontend changes that were initially added while\ninvestigating the ticket, keeping the final PR scoped to the\nauthorization requirement.\n* No changes were made to the Customer Portal authentication flow.\n\n## Does this use the v2 API?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThis change only affects Angular frontend route authorization and does\nnot use the v2 API.\n\n## Does this add a new communication between services?:\n\n**No.**\n\nThere is no new communication between services. This PR only changes\nfrontend route guard behavior.\n\n## Before and After UI (Required for UI-impacting PRs)\n\n**Not applicable.**\n\nThis PR does not introduce or modify the visual UI. The change affects\nroute access/authorization only.\n\n## Dev notes (Optional)\n\nThe final functional change is limited to the Employee Portal route in\n`app.routes.ts`.\n\n\n## Linked pull requests (Optional)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqunCVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfw4QAJ+4gFjb1